\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sit tight as market awaits fresh cues. \b0\par\par\uc2 989 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2001\par 03:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sat pat \par \par \uc2  in their recent ranges early on Tuesday with fading local \par \par \uc2  factors forcing the market to await fresh cues. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen        failed to provide much guidance, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attention on the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was more focused on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Investors were keeping an eye on preliminary second quarter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. productivity data due later on Tuesday to gauge how weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economy may be.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the recent bailing out of long U.S. dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the Singapore dollar and North Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tapered off, investors were not yet keen on rebuilding their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long U.S. dollar positions. That could leave regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trapped in familiar territory.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the long term, analysts say the U.S. dollar should\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resume its climb against the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Asia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery depends on the U.S. picking up first.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar declined to make any drastic moves,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and was expected to consolidate around the 1.7800-1.7850 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said with activity on the dollar/yen subdued, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market found little motivation to test the dollar/Sing in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par either direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts showed the dollar/Sing was in oversold territory,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with a 14-day relative strength index reading of 28.741,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicating the Sing dollar had room for downwards correction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht was locked in a narrow range as most players were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par done with dollar unwinding linked to Prime Minister Thaksin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shinawatra's court victory on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trapped between dollar bids\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from oil firms and importers at 45.30 and offers from U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par names and exporters at 45.40-45.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Given a dearth of fresh leads, the market was awaiting the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulations which are expected soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht funding costs eased slightly, with the tom/next rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted at -0.20/0.15 satang per dollar in both the offshore and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won eased on the local stock stock market's lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opening and as players covered their short dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the won's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said the market was also cautious ahead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the Bank of Korea's monetary policy meeting on Thursday with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts divided on whether key interest rates will be lowered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The BOK last cut its overnight call rate by 25 basis points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 4.75 percent in July as inflationary pressure seemed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ease.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won's downside was expected to be limited on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export-related inflows and settlement of stocks bought by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar edged down in subdued trade ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par July trade data due at 0245 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said sentiment towards the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par took a hit from a weaker Nasdaq close, which would put pressure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the local stock market. Foreign investors sold on Monday a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par net T$22.74 million worth of local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll showed economists expect July exports to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fall 23.7 percent on the year and imports to shrink by 32.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Inflation data issued on Monday sparked hopes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may further lower key interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The consumer price index in July rose 0.11 percent on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year while wholesale price index fell 0.22 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso barely moved from Monday's local close of 53.22,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and was expected to stick within a 53.15-53.30 range as it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued to be plagued by poor sentiment amid a dearth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Manila dealers said local corporate dollar demand was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to emerge past 53.20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They added while the market has largely shrugged off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments from President Gloria Arroyo warning of stricter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par controls on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade, players were watching the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We think it's just verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . They don't want to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, they just don't have the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves," said a European bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah drifted in a quiet market as the market watched\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out for the new cabinet line-up expected to be announced on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, more than two weeks after President Megawati\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sukarnoputri came to power.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "While the market may not have high hopes, there are still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential surprises to the downside like further delays and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par naming of some past perpetrators from (Suharto's regime)," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par IDEAglobal.com.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was weighed by corporate demand for the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 9,340-9,350, Jakarta dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was concerned over the country's lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par progress in privatisation. The government said on Monday it had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par no plans to revise its revenue target for privatisations in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2001, despite raising nothing so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It has targeted privatisation revenue of 6.5 trillion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah ($695 million) in fiscal 2001 (January-December), but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par several sales have been delayed by a weak market and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par difficulties.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0143 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.85       124.06         +0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.7842       1.7815         -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.665       34.650         -0.04\par  Korean won   1287.00      1288.00         +0.08\par  Baht           45.48        45.41         -0.15\par  Peso           53.23        53.22         -0.02\par  Rupiah       9280.00      9350.00         +0.75\par  Ringgit  