\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen lends steadying hand. \b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2001\par 03:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 26 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held fast \par \par \uc2  to their recent ranges early on Thursday, looking to capitalise \par \par \uc2  on the limping dollar. \par \par \uc2      Poor corporate earnings and concerns over the U.S. economy \par \par \uc2  continued to nag the dollar, despite Treasury Secretary Paul \par \par \uc2  O'Neill's committment to the strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Both the yen        and euro        racked up gains against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar, with the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefitting from hopes for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a rate cut from the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may tag along with the yen's move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher, dealers and analysts said the doubts plaguing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar do not bode well for Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Export-dependent Asia needs to see signs of a pick-up in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its largest market, the United States, to stage a recovery,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was trying to strengthen above 1.8160,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though dealers said dollar bids were lurking around 1.8150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said players had been unloading their dollar longs,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the market still jittery over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But they added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not spotted in the market on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was eyeing the dollar/yen with further gains by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen expected to spark a test of 1.8150, where dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss dollar sell orders were clustered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won edged up on the Nasdaq's rise and a higher yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But trading was likely to remain thin ahead of June\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industrial production and current account numbers and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first-half trade data due on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts expect an average 0.4 percent month-on-month fall\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in production due to depressed exports, according to a Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poll.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With the import season in full swing, the peso stayed under\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure, but players were cautious on an expected hike in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commercial bank reserve requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight rates were likely to remain unchanged this week but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising reserve requirements would be considered when the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank's monetary board meets on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The overnight borrowing rate is currently at nine percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the lending rate is at 11.25 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A hike of one percent in reserve requirements results in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mopping up of 12 to 13 billion pesos, leaving banks with less\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cash in the interbank market, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht benefited slightly from the Sing dollar's rise,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though it was unable to decisively break 45.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said trade in the dollar/baht remained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par subdued as off-shore players were still concerned over new\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reporting rules aimed at staving off speculation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Comments from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par failed to move sentiment. He said the bank was committed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allowing market forces move the baht, but would step in to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prevent too much volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah stayed below the 10,000 mark as some uncertainty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerged over the country's political picture.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The top assembly will choose the country's next vice\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par president later at 0200 GMT after two rounds of voting failed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to produce a result on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders saw more room for the rupiah to correct lower as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par charts showed the dollar was still massively oversold.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The IMF said it expected its executive board to discuss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lending for Indonesia at the end of August or in early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     If the board completes the review of the country's reform\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par efforts it would pave the way for the resumption of a stalled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $5 billion loan programme Indonesia badly needs to restore its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar extended an upswing to 34.80 from 34.85\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late on Wednesday, thanks to the firmer yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei stocks         enjoyed modest gains on top of a 2.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent rise in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chilling the mood was Taiwan's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which hit an all time high of over US$35 billion at the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par June, up 75.1 percent from a year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0123 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.52       124.35         +0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.8157       1.8169         +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.814       34.850         +0.10\par  Korean won   1300.00      1310.00         +0.77\par  Baht           45.70        45.75         +0.11\par  Peso           53.63        53.60         -0.06\par  Rupiah      10050.00     10000.00         -0.50\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.