\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sluggish as market begs for fresh cues. \b0\par\par\uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2001\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trod familiar ground late on Wednesday as the market rooted around for fresh trading cues. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said with the yen failing to give much direction and Hong Kong markets closed due to a typhoon, most players were content to hold their fire for now. \par \par \uc2  However, the market was still keeping close tabs on the dollar/yen following U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill's repeated committment to the strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  On the local front, the Singapore dollar shrugged off the government's off-budget measures to shore up the economy. \par \par \uc2  And the initial euphoria over Indonesia's peaceful change of power settled down, as players in Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets woke up to what little attention global investors are actually paying to the country. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar settled around the 1.8160 level after hitting a high of 1.8153 when foreign funds were dumping their dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they have been suspected of doing since it announced a change in its Sing dollar policy on July 12. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said there was no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, and players were unwinding their dollar positions with the aim of building them up again around 1.8150. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah kept within 9,800-10,000 for most of the session, only briefly weakening to touch a session low of 10,075. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said sporadic dollar offers from state banks kept most players on the sidelines but strong dollar demand was spotted around 9,800. \par \par \uc2  Overall the market was in a wait-and-see mood pondering as the new government and economic team took shape. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was too premature to lower domestic interest rates on the back of the recent rupiah spike and would wait another couple of weeks before making a decision. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was stuck in a tight 1,306.8-1,310.4 range in cautious trade ahead of June current account balance and industrial output and first half trade data due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said exporters' dollar inflows limited the won's downside while uncertainty about the yen and a weak local stock market capped gains. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed economists expect industrial production to shrink for the third consecutive month in June, with an average forecast of a 0.4 percent fall mainly on sagging exports. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said weak economic numbers were likely to pressure the won towards the 1,320 mark, seen last on April 30. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was wedged in a tight 45.69-45.76 range in lacklustre trade with players reluctant to take aggressive positions on worries over new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade reporting rules. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said stricter rules, aimed at discouraging speculation by foreigners holding baht bank deposits, would be placed for the governor's approval this week. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Thailand had no plans to impose capital controls or return the baht to a fixed exchange rate and had no intention to raise domestic interest rates. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  Trading on the peso moved sluggishly with players complaining about the dearth of fresh factors. \par \par \uc2  However, Manila dealers said sentiment towards the peso was still hobbled by the country's poor economic fundamentals and bleak external environment. \par \par \uc2  "The attitude around here is hoard dollars while you can," said a local bank dealer in Manila. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank would likely keep overnight rates steady, but may consider raising commercial bank's reserve requirements. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar crept higher as a bounce in local stocks fuelled hopes of foreign investment equity-related inflows. \par \par \uc2  But given how poorly Taiwan's economy is doing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the local dollar's rise to around 34.80 to keep its export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan saw some badly needed good news on the macroeconomic front. June M2 money supply grew by 6.01 percent on year, compared to May's 5.61 percent growth, which was a record low. That pick-up hinted at an increase in investment and lending. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0934 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.36       124.15         -0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.8178       1.8180         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.850       34.878         +0.08\par  Korean won   1310.00      1309.00         -0.08\par  Baht           45.72        45.71         -0.02\par  Peso           53.60        53.55         -0.08\par  Rupiah       9950.00      9825.00         -1.26\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par