\par\par \b \uc2  MAS Lee Says To Guard Against Singapore Dlr Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2001\par 05:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will continue to "guard against destabilizing speculation in the Singapore dollar," MAS Chairman Lee Hsien Loong said Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS' primary objective over the medium term is to maintain price stability and the purchasing power of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Lee told participants at a conference marking the MAS' 30th anniversary. \par \par \uc2  By pursuing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy through a "managed float" of the Singapore dollar, the MAS can buffer the effects on the economy of short-term financial volatility, and avoid sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  misalignments that could damage the export sector, Lee said. \par \par \uc2  "Managing the float requires us to lean against the wind at times, but provided our exchange rate policy is aligned with economic fundamentals, and our ability and determination to counter destabilizing speculation is not in doubt, we need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less than might be expected." \par \par \uc2  Until recently, the MAS didn't reveal its view of the Singapore dollar exchange rate, or its policy intentions. But the MAS has adopted a more transparent approach to help the market and general public understand the MAS policy stance better, Lee said. With less uncertainty, policy implementation will be more effective, he added. \par \par \uc2  The MAS was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably demonstrating its resolve to defend the Singapore dollar, even though it shifted its monetary policy on July 1 to a neutral position from a bias toward a gradual appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With the market heavily long in U.S. dollars, it was even more compelling for the MAS - which has been making its presence felt recently - to step in, market watchers said. \par \par \uc2  Regarding banking regulation, Lee said the MAS is adopting a "risk-focused, consolidated approach" to supervision. \par \par \uc2  "We will place more emphasis on understanding and evaluating an institution's risk management systems and internal controls," he told conference participants. \par \par \uc2  On the subject of corporate governance, Lee said the MAS will continue to push for higher standards, particularly on enhancing the independence of boards and institutionalizing professional management. \par \par \uc2  "But this must be phased in judiciously. We cannot impose these standards in a vacuum without regard to the institutional and cultural realities in our corporate sector." \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 415-4045; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010720dx7k0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
