\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Find cheer as dollar sulks. \b0\par\par\uc2 903 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2001\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 19 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lurched towards firmer ground early Thursday as the market pounced on the dollar following remarks from President George Bush and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan. \par \par \uc2  Bush ushered dollar bears into the market by telling reporters the strong dollar threatened U.S. exports but Teasury Secretary Paul O'Neill later said the U.S. still backed its long-standing strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar found little solace in Greenspan's semi-annual congressional testimony as the Fed chairman warned the U.S. economy faced a range of hurdles and more interest rate cuts may be needed. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed primary dealers unanimously expecting another 25 basis point cut when the Fed next meets on August 21. \par \par \uc2  Double click or for the full poll. \par \par \uc2  But the bounce regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were enjoying may be short-lived as Asia's economic fortunes are bound to the U.S. Wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is holding players back from properly trouncing the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso took a gasp of air as players unwound some of their long dollar positions after talk on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through two foreign banks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the dollar/peso was due for a slight correction, with its 14-day relative strength index showing the dollar in overbought territory since June 15. Its reading on Thursday was 85. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they were still looking to snatch up dollars on dips, given the gloomy economic outlook for the Philippines coupled with the dearth of dollars. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  President Bush's dollar comments lifted the won to 1,302 in New York. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at 1,305 in the onshore market on Thursday, against the Wednesday's close of 1,311.7. \par \par \uc2  But gains were expected to be capped by Greenspan's cautious outlook on the U.S. economy, which is a major market for Korean exports. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said 1,300.00 should remain a solid barrier for the won to crack as players are likely to buy the dollar on dips to that level. \par \par \uc2  The one-month won in the non-deliverable forward market was quoted at 1,314/1,315 and three-month at 1,319/1,320. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was off its overnight low of 45.81 on the back of a firmer yen, but the upside was limited by hedging activity and political concerns. \par \par \uc2  Consitutional court judges denied reports by local media the court may deliver a verdict in Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's graft case as early as next week. \par \par \uc2  "It's every one's guess what the outcome would be, and the market is reluctant to pare long dollar positions," said a dealer in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  "Also, investors people are quite active in hedging against baht losses despite high swap points. That added selling pressure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The baht remained trapped in the dollar's uptrend channel dating back to June 26. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar extended gains to 1.8280 having popped above 1.83 overnight for the first time in more than a week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said interbank players liquidated their long dollar positions, triggering some stop-loss U.S. dollar selling orders at 1.8300. But they emphasised there was no particular catalyst for the latest Sing dollar rise besides the steadier yen and said it might resume its downtrend after pulling back to around 1.8265-50. INDONESIAN RUPIAH The rupiah held onto gains at two-week highs around 11,265, as banks liquidated their dollar long positions in thin trading. But Jakarta dealers said the outlook was not so rosy given concerns about rising political tension. President Abdurrahman Wahid said he would declare a state of emergency and call early elections if his enemies try to oust him. \par \par \uc2  Top legislators are calling for bringing forward impeachment hearings against President Wahid from the scheduled date of August 1. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar trading around the key psychological level of 35.00, underpinned by the dollar's retreat against the yen and wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened slightly higher at 34.983 against the Thursday's close of 35.027 before dipping to 35.025. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it around 35.00 amid downward pressure from the ailing domestic stock market, and poor economic outlook. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0231 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.97       125.35         +1.11\par  Sing dlr      1.8284       1.8321         +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    35.049       35.027         -0.06\par  Korean won   1304.00      1311.00         +0.54\par  Baht           45.72        45.79         +0.15\par  Peso 