\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Investors run for dollar cover. \b0\par\par\uc2 927 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2001\par 04:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 17 (Reuters) - Domestic woes and \par \par \uc2  Argentina's economic crisis ruffled Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, with the wobbly yen providing more distress. \par \par \uc2      "Risk aversity is pretty high right now. All in all it's a \par \par \uc2  pretty dire environment and the slowness of the U.S. recovery \par \par \uc2  is not helping much. Investors are on the defensive," said a \par \par \uc2  dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He added the region's dependence on its exports coupled \par \par \uc2  with the still-sluggish U.S. economy left most Asian countries \par \par \uc2  with little choice but to accept weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Singapore will release June non-oil export figures at 0530 \par \par \uc2  GMT, which analysts expect to show another slump due to the \par \par \uc2  electronics downturn. \par \par \uc2  The market was keeping tabs on the latest developments in \par \par \uc2  Argentina, where the government is seeking support for an \par \par \uc2  austerity plan to prevent a debt default. \par \par \uc2  Investors were also focused on Federal Reserve Chairman \par \par \uc2  Alan Greenspan's congressional testimony on Wednesday and U.S. \par \par \uc2  data, including industrial production and capacity utilisation \par \par \uc2  later Tuesday, and consumer price data on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Markets in Seoul were closed for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso slid to fresh six-month lows of 53.84, but trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained thin with only $2 million transacted by 0137 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It lost more than half a centavo on Thursday after foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks placed arbitrage orders between the spot and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward market to cover offshore dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Manila dealers said they were buying dollars on the spot\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market from 53.25 and selling the one-week dollar/peso NDF at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par premium of 53.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the premium was unusually high compared with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par normal 7-10 centavos as the dollar/peso NDF shot up on concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about the domestic economy and possible spillover from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Argentina.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the one-week dollar/peso NDF was quoted at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 53.95/54.05.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the peso would breach 54 soon but fears of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would halt its fall around 54.50.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar steered a steady course as wariness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held speculators at bay.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said local banks were interested in selling dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.8390, sparking talk that they may be acting on behalf\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But they added local corporate dollar demand for hedging\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purposes provided firm support for the dollar around 1.8355.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     June non-oil exports due out later in the day were expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to extend their sharp decline, and could dampen the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's prospects further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht ground lower alongside the yen and other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but high baht funding costs and fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped limit the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said there was talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par entered the market to shore up the baht around 45.70 on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, with regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heading south, they added\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they did not expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be aggressive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no shortage of negative news on the local front.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government on Monday slashed its 2001 export growth target,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par changing it to a range of minus 1.2 to zero percent from its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous forecast of 9.46 percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht funding costs remained high in the offshore market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with tom/next rate quoted at 0/1.5 satang per dollar and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-month rate quoted at 36/48 satang.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was in a stupor at 11,330 with dealers keeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an wary eye on rising political tension.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The head of Indonesia's highest legislature said the body\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would meet informally on Friday for a snap impeachment session\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if President Wahid declared a state of emergency and held early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elections.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The People's Consultative Assembly is scheduled to convene\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a special session on August 1 to hear Wahid account for his\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 20-month rule and consider impeaching him.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market was also eyeing developments over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the possible release of a frozen $400 million loan from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par IMF.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar retained its weak tone, but wariness of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to keep the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a tight range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It opened at 35.002 against the Monday's close of 35.006,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but soon slipped to the morning low of 35.072 on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar bids from corporate hedgers and importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As with the Thai baht and the Singapore dollar, the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar remains supported and the market continues to see the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par test of 35.300 being the next target," said a report from UBS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Warburg.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0152 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.34       124.88         -0.37\par  Sing dlr      1.8363       1.8375         +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    35.053       35.006         -0.13\par  Korean won   1305.00      1308.00         +0.23\par  Baht           45.73        45.73         +0.00\par  Peso           53.86        53.71         -0.28\par  Rupiah      11338.00     11336.00         -0.02\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.34       114.45         -8.69\par  Sing dlr      1.8363       1.7365         -5.43\par  Taiwan dlr    35.053       32.900         -6.14\par  Korean won   1305.00      1277.00         -2.15\par  Baht           45.73        43.70         -4.44\par  Peso           53.86        50.75         -5.77\par  Rupiah      11338.00      9470.00        -16.48\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010717dx7h004bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
