\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore stocks close firmer, techs up on Nasdaq. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Joyce Liu \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 12 (Reuters) - Singapore stocks ended a touch higher on Thursday on a lack of market-moving news but technology shares firmed modestly in line with the Nasdaq's gains. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Straits Times Index ended up 0.69 percent at 1,672.81 points. Turnover was 486 million shares against Wednesday's 341 million. \par \par \uc2  There was little impact from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement that it had shifted to a neutral exchange rate policy in line with the sharp downturn in the city state's trade-driven economy. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar sank to fresh 11-year lows near 1.84 to the U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement but bounced back after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It was at 1.8335/45 at 0945 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The electronics sector index jumped 2.21 percent with help from Motorola Inc and Yahoo! , both of which posted quarterly results that edged ahead of analysts' consensus estimates. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the MAS shift could help export-oriented firms, especially technology companies, expecting a weak local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports. \par \par \uc2  But more argued that a slightly weaker Sing dollar would barely help to counter the electronics sector's high inventory levels and the global slowdown. \par \par \uc2  Lingering worries over the local economy should keep the market weak, although no major movements were expected after dismal growth numbers on Tuesday and gloomy government projections on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The bearish data has been factored into the market pretty much. Investors in Singapore are bearish but they are prepared for the worst outcome," said Nicholas Yeo, an investment manager at Aberdeen Asset Management. \par \par \uc2  "The market is at its oversold levels now." \par \par \uc2  Trade Minister George Yeo told parliament on Wednesday unemployment was likely to worsen in the second half, when economic growth may come in between minus one and plus one percent. \par \par \uc2  This came one day after Singapore slipped into recession with anaemic second quarter gross domestic product data. The government also revised its growth forecast for 2001 to 0.5 to 1.5 percent from 3.5 to 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Top net gainer Venture Manufacturing rose 2.36 percent to S$13.00, followed by OCBC Bank which gained 2.56 percent to S$12.00. \par \par \uc2  Yeo remained conservative on the tech and banking sectors, expecting more earnings warnings from tech firms and little growth room for banks. \par \par \uc2  NatSteel Ltd was one of the biggest net losers with a fall of 2.75 percent to S$1.06. \par \par \uc2  The diversified steel miller said on Thursday it would post a loss in the first half of the year and lay off about a fifth of the workers at its Singapore steel plant due to continued weakness in the local construction sector. \par \par \uc2  This came after its unit NatSteel Broadway warned on Wednesday its interim results would be crimped by the global electronics downturn. \par \par \uc2  The contract manufacturer rebounded five cents to end at S$2.41 after sinking to a four-week low on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Despite earnings warnings, market watchers expect to see activity in small and medium-sized electronics firms amid merger and acquisition speculation. \par \par \uc2  Top active Fu Yu Manufacturing , a plastic injection moulder maker, surged 31.46 percent to S$0.585 in hectic volume of 52.5 million shares, buoyed by rumours it would be acquired by a global electronics contract manufacturer. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00gua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
