\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Singapore dlr move pragmatic due to recession. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jacqueline Wong \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 12 (Reuters) - Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a pragmatic and surprise shift to a neutral exchange rate policy on Thursday as the city state's trade-driven economy slides into recession. \par \par \uc2  The move, designed to keep the Singapore dollar steady on a trade-weighted basis rather on a gradually appreciating trend, effectively is an easing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary stance. \par \par \uc2  "This is pragmatic given the sharp slowdown. The economy is already in recession and the second half will still be in recession," said ABN AMRO Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Gerard Teo. \par \par \uc2  "They announced it saying this is the stance now - it doesn't mean they did not change it earlier." \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hit 11-year lows near 1.84 to the U.S. dollar after the announcement but bounced back sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  By 0830 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1.8359/69. \par \par \uc2  WEAK ECONOMY PROMPTS CHANGE \par \par \uc2  While most central banks use interest rates as their main tool, the MAS tightens or loosens monetary conditions in the economy primarily by steering the value of the local dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS had maintained a bias of gradual and modest appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a trade-weighted basis since early 2000 as the region came out of the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  But it said it was making the change against the backdrop of a weaker external economic environment and as near-term growth prospects for the Singapore economy turned gloomier. \par \par \uc2  "Economic activity slowed much more in the first half of 2001 than was expected, causing market sentiment to shift against the Singapore dollar," Tharman Shanmugaratnam, managing director of the MAS, told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "MAS has therefore shifted to a neutral exchange rate policy stand, with a policy band centred on a zero percent appreciation of the S$ Neer (nominal effective exchange rate)." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to guide the S$ Neer within the policy band and stood ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  SURPRISE AT SHIFT \par \par \uc2  "The shift to a neutral stance wasn't priced in by many people. Some banks were still calling for a no change, although we were thinking they would shift," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas. "I think it really opens up 1.85 now." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said inflationary pressures were subsiding and it expected inflation as measured by the consumer price index to trend lower to the 1.0-1.5 percent range for 2001 as a whole. \par \par \uc2  Shanmugaratnam said the Sing dollar's slide was due partly to concerns of a weakening economy but also to a stronger U.S. dollar. Strong demand for the U.S. dollar to fund mergers and acquisitions by local corporations contributed to the weakness. \par \par \uc2  But Shanmugaratnam noted that the current slowdown reflected a decline in demand, not an erosion of competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "There is no reason for any persistent weakening of the Singapore dollar," he said. \par \par \uc2  GDP TO WEAKEN FURTHER \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the shift in monetary stance ought to ease the impact of the downturn on Singapore's manufacturing economy. \par \par \uc2  "When you have a slowdown, all competing economies' exchange rates are also depreciating so you really cannot be standing still," said Eddie Lee, strategist with Vickers Ballas. \par \par \uc2  But the exchange rate has also become less of an issue among manufacturers than before as they are more concerned about price competition, productivity and other costs, Lee said. \par \par \uc2  Dismal advance second quarter growth data on Tuesday fuelled fears the city state was heading for tougher times. \par \par \uc2  Singapore entered a recession as gross domestic product contracted 0.8 percent on year in the April to June quarter and dropped 10.1 percent on an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis. \par \par \uc2  The poor data prompted the government to revise its growth forecast for 2001 to 0.5 to 1.5 percent from 3.5 to 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "I am slightly surprised but the (MAS) decision is well justified by the recent economic data," said Julian Jessop, global markets economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  "We suspect they have been allowing the Sing dollar to depreciate on a trade-weighted basis so 1.86 should be a reasonable cap for now." \par \par \uc2  (With reporting by Joyce Liu and Sonali Desai). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00gef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
