\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Sing dlr bounces off 11-yr low on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 07:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar bounced back sharply from a fresh 11-year low around 1.84 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar lost half a cent immediately after interbank players scrambled to sell following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's (MAS) surprise shift in stance to neutral from tightening in its half-yearly policy review statement. \par \par \uc2  "The shift to neutral stance wasn't priced in by many people... they have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.84," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  The MAS had maintained a bias of gradual and modest appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a trade-weighted basis since early 2000 as the region came out of the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  The MAS does not reveal the make-up of the trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the U.S. dollar aggressively through local banks, pushing the Sing dollar back to 1.8345. \par \par \uc2  When contacted by Reuters, the MAS said it did not normally comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS said in its policy statement it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  "But the MAS has said that the Sing dollar has already shifted down to the lower half of the band, so if it hits the bottom end, we can expect the MAS to come in to support the Sing dollar," BNP's Thio said. \par \par \uc2  "Still if you think that the rest of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro and the yen will stay weak then on a trade-weighted basis, the Sing dollar should continue to depreciate on a nominal basis. Certainly the first target is 1.85 for us. We think that should be achieved quite shortly." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited further declines for the time being but many were still looking to buy U.S. dollars on dips from 1.8300 and 1.8330. \par \par \uc2  "We are moving our view on the Sing dollar to 1.86 (from 1.84) in the next three months," said Julian Jessop, global markets economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar has been under sustained downward pressure since the start of the year on persistent fears of ebbing growth as a slowing global economy eats into exports. \par \par \uc2  Advance GDP growth fell 0.8 percent year-on-year in the second quarter and dropped 10.1 percent on an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis, leaving the city state in a technical recession. \par \par \uc2  In its policy review statement, the MAS said inflation pressures were subsiding with the consumer price index to head lower to 1.0-1.5 percent for 2001. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's CPI rose 1.9 percent in May from a year earlier but fell 0.4 percent compared with April. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00a19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
