\par\par \b \uc2  US Dlr Drops To 1.8346 Vs Singapore Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2001\par 04:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. dollar has fallen below S$1.8350 Wednesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after it rose to a new 11-year high of S$1.8377 Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0247 GMT, (10:47 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8343.\par - - 11/07/01 02-59G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  A European bank, believed to be acting on behalf of the MAS, started unloading U.S. dollars around the S$1.8365 to S$1.8370 level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It appears to be pretty aggressive," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's weakness it providing a floor for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which remains supported above S$1.8340 for now, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the U.S. dollar was quoted at Y125.72, higher than Y125.35 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's worsening economic outlook has hammered the local dollar, sending it to 11-year lows. \par \par \uc2  Advance, or flash, gross domestic product estimates issued Tuesday were worse than economists had expected, accelerating the Singapore dollar's fall. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's economy contracted an annualized 10.1% in the second quarter from the first quarter. After an 11.3% annualized quarter-on-quarter drop in the January-March period, Singapore meets the conventional definition of a recession - two back-to-back quarters of economic contraction on a quarter-on-quarter basis. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore government consequently slashed its 2001 GDP growth forecast to 0.5%-1.5%, from April's 3.5%-5.5% estimate. \par \par \uc2  Market participants expect the government to provide hints on an expected stimulus package to help resuscitate the economy when Parliament meets later in the day. \par \par \uc2  As well, most economists expect the MAS to reaffirm its policy of allowing a gradual, modest appreciation of the Singapore dollar against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its major trading partners and key competitors, when it announces the results of its biannual policy review Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the MAS is probably also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar had slipped further to S$1.8338 at 0324 GMT (11.24 p.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely descend further toward S$1.8300, while noting that the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has prompted several participants to bail out of their long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But a lot of people are waiting to buy U.S. dollars below S$1.8300,"\par said a dealer at a European bank.\par    -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 11/07/01 03-34G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx7b0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
