\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Earnings woes dog region, typhoon blasts HK trade. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, July 6 (Reuters) - Earnings fears sent Asian \par \par \uc2  asset prices sagging to a lower close with Hong Kong stocks \par \par \uc2  suffering a particularly soggy end to the week after Typhoon \par \par \uc2  Utor blew shut the territory's financial markets on Friday. \par \par \uc2      The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong cancelled all trade on \par \par \uc2  Friday as the heavy tropical storm lashed the south China coast \par \par \uc2  and kept the bond, gold and money markets shut. \par \par \uc2      Malaysian equities shone through an otherwise gloomy day as \par \par \uc2  the benchmark Kuala Lumpur Composite Index climbed an \par \par \uc2  impressive 1.6 percent to mark its highest close in three \par \par \uc2  months. \par \par \uc2      Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped restrain dollar \par \par \uc2  bulls in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets although the Japanese yen's \par \par \uc2   sustained losses below 125 pointed to a bearish outlook. \par \par \uc2      Tokyo stocks skidded for the third straight day with the \par \par \uc2  benchmark Nikkei 225 finishing 2.4 percent off at a \par \par \uc2  three-and-a-half month low, hit by weakness in Sony and other \par \par \uc2  high-tech bellwethers after profit warnings abroad rekindled \par \par \uc2  nagging earnings worries at home. \par \par \uc2      MALAYSIA STOCKS SHINE THROUGH \par \par \uc2      Malaysian stocks extended a recent run-up as comparatively \par \par \uc2  cheap valuations continued to attract investors back to one of \par \par \uc2  the year's worst-performing markets in Asia. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark Composite Index         ended up 1.6 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the day -- it's highest close since April 3 -- and 5.7\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent higher over the course of the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Malaysian stock market had been one of regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par laggards this year -- down 7.8 percent so far -- but at current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels, it is trading around 12 times earnings for 2001, below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an average of 20 times in the past 10 years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Malaysia is not drop-dead gorgeous but attractive enough\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to warrant some interest in it," said Johan Tazrin Ngo, who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helps manage 80 million ringgit ($21 million) at Kenanga\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investment Management.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CRUNCHED BY DOLLAR STRENGTH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar hit fresh 11-year lows of 1.8285 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedge fund selling but quickly bounced back on wariness of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following rumours the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS) had stepped in in overseas trade on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talk also echoed in the peso and rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets, while Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was active again in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defending the 34.50 per U.S. dollar mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the region, next week's major events include Singapore's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par preliminary second-quarter growth data on Tuesday and the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy statement on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some market players said the Sing dollar's weakness was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largely in line with the yen and other regionals and estimated\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that levels around 1.8325 would be a threshold for the MAS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some economists argue GDP figures, due on Tuesday, would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely show another downturn, prompting the MAS to shift its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias to neutral from tightening to weather the slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Next week there will be a big announcement coming out from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the MAS and I wouldn't be surprised if the MAS was to subtlely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signal to the market that there would be a bias towards a less\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par restrictive monetary stance," Steve Xu, regional economist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SG Securities in Hong Kong said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Therefore dollar against Sing is likely to reach S$1.85,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Xu told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said the Taiwan dollar and the Korean won were also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par facing pressure from the overwhelming strength of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "In the near term, we suspect three economies -- Taiwan,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea and Singapore because they do not have an external debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overhang - are going to devalue their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  quite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharply," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended off lows after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters offered dollars when the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was just a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whisker away from the key psychological support of 34.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I suspect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of China in Taiwan will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par engineer a one-off devaluation very soon, probably to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 35-36 level against the dollar," Xu said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL STOCKS DOWNCAST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korean shares underperformed the region on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the benchmark KOSPI sinking 2.5 percent as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technology shares were hit hard by profit warnings from global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tech giants such as Britain's Marconi and U.S. Advanced\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Micro Devices (AMD) .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chipmakers such as Samsung Electronics and Hynix\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Semiconductor suffered after microchip maker AMD\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par warned its fiscal second-quarter earnings would be a fraction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of what Wall Street had forecast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIAN BOND TRADE BLOWN OUT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian dollar bond spreads drifted slightly wider on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as trade was all but blown away in Hong Kong by Typhoon Utor,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which kept financial markets closed and dealing rooms silent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's nobody trading here today. The market is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par officially closed so it's pretty quiet. It may pick up when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par London opens later," a dealer at a U.S. bank in Hong Kong said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As it is stands, we're probably a few basis points wider\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the benchmarks, but nothing's trading," a dealer at a U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank in Hong Kong said. "The market is officially closed so\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it's pretty quiet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recent issues were quoted wider after overnight trade, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malaysia's $1 billion 2011 bonds about five basis points wider\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than at the close of Asian trade on Thursday at about 250 bps\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over Treasuries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippine Finance Secretary Jose Camacho said in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par statement on Friday the government had mandated Credit Suisse\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par First Boston as its sole book runner for its forthcoming $500\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million sovereign bond issue.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0937 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.77       125.41         -0.29\par  Sing dlr      1.8256       1.8252         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr     34.42        34.44         +0.06\par  Korean won   1289.00      1296.40         +0.57\par  Baht           45.40        45.45         +0.11\par  Peso           52.86        52.85         -0.02\par  Rupiah      11335.00     11355.00         +0.18\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japa