\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Cushioned by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,050 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 6 (Reuters) - Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped restrain dollar bulls in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday although the yen's sustained losses below 125 pointed to a bearish outlook. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar hit fresh 11-year lows of 1.8285 on hedge fund selling but quickly bounced back on wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped in in overseas trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was well-supported offshore after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured to have sold at least $100 million in both spot and forward markets to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day. Thai markets were closed on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk also echoed in the peso and rupiah markets, while Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was active again in defending the 34.50 per U.S. dollar mark. \par \par \uc2  The market will be focused on the U.S. June jobs report due out at 1230 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters forecast nonfarm payrolls fell 44,000 in June after May's 19,000 drop. \par \par \uc2  In the region, next week's major events include Singapore's preliminary second quarter growth data on Tuesday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy statement on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  Baht trading was thinned by a holiday in Thailand, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held above 45.40 after Thursday's rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed baht funding costs in the offshore market sharply higher. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate shot up to 41/49 satang per dollar from around 10/14 satang earlier this week, making it expensive to hold the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was also supported by a Financial Times report quoting Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula as saying he intended to manage the baht more actively. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar suffered a volatile session, stumbling to fresh 11-year lows of 1.8285 before bouncing back to 1.8250 as a U.S. bank and a local bank took profits on their dollar longs ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did exist but some said the Sing dollar's weakness was largely in line with the yen and other regionals. They estimated levels around 1.8325 would be a threshold for the MAS. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts argue GDP figures, due on Tuesday, would likely show another downturn, prompting the MAS to shift its bias to neutral from tightening to weather the slowdown. \par \par \uc2  "With the economy contracting sharply and inflation low, the MAS is likely to have a bias for a weaker Sing dollar," Ron Leven, chief Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers said in a research note. He expects the Sing dollar to reach 1.90-1.95 in the first quarter of next year. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso kept to a narrow 52.92-52.94 range in listless trade, with volume of only $73.5 million against Thursday's $111.06 million. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said companies were still looking to buy dollars as the peso's stumble to 5-= month lows of 53.10 on Wednesday encouraged corporate treasurers to hedge their dollar requirements for the second half of 2001. But both banks and corporates became cautious after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials asked them to use the non-deliverable forward market to cover future dollar needs. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines' gross international reserves rose to $14.58 billion at the end of June from $14.44 billion a month before. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended off lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and exporters offered dollars when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was just a whisker away from the key psychological support of 34.50. \par \par \uc2  It was pressured by a weaker yen and there was also no shortage of negative news to worsen its outlook. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters predicted June exports fell an average 18.95 percent on the year to US$10.03 billion and imports slid even further by 22.79 percent to $8.91 billion. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won kept steady around 1,295 on expected foreign direct investment flows and hopes Thursday's rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help the economy bottom out later in the year. \par \par \uc2  Data from home and abroad also helped sentiment, including the U.S. NAPM non-manufacturing business survey which showed economic activity may be turning around. \par \par \uc2  Foreign direct investment in Korea rose 16.8 percent on the year in the first half of 2001 but investment plans from U.S. and Japanese firms were down 26.4 and 61.6 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  But dealers saw the won as vulnerable to a weakening yen and selling of local stocks by foreign investors amid more profit warnings from U.S. tech companies. INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was stuck within a tight 11,330-11,350 range amid thin conditions as corporates and interbank players stayed out of the market on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta reported little activity by state banks whose dollar sales on Thursday sparked talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid repeated his threat to declare a state of emergency if his opponents pushed ahead with efforts to oust him through an impeachment hearing. \par \par \uc2  Parliament is due to start a special impeachment session on August 1, which Wahid terms extra-constitutional. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile senior officials expressed confidence a deal on resumption of lending with the IMF would be reached in a week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0854 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.76       125.41         -0.28\par  Sing dlr      1.8257       1.8252         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.473       34.465         -0.02\par  Korean won   1294.00      1296.40         +0.19\par  Baht           45.36        45.45         +0.20\par  Peso           52.86        52.98         +0.23\par  Rupiah      11335.00     11355.00         +0.18\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.76       114.45         -8.99\par  Sing dlr      1.8257       1.7365         -4.89\par  Taiwan dlr    34.473       32.900         -4.56\par  Korean won   1294.00      1277.00         -1.31\par  Baht           45.36        43.70         -3.66\par  Peso           52.86        50.75         -3.99\par  Rupiah      11335.00      9470.00        -16.45\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc