\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen saps regionals, baht shines. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,095 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2001\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were dragged lower in late trade on Thursday as the yen's sustained losses beyond 125 heightened concerns about competitive devaluation and capital outflows. \par \par \uc2  Only the Thai baht bucked the trend, racking up good gains after rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent players stumbling to cover short baht positions. \par \par \uc2  The yen was weighed by comments by Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda on Wednesday that he would not resist a weaker yen as long as it reflected fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Investors fear a weaker yen could jeopardise Japan's ability to absorb imports from the rest of Asia, make its exports cheaper in other markets, and prompt some Japanese lenders to recall their loans from Asian debtors. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro hit seven-month lows against the dollar on expectations the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave rates unchanged later in the day despite evidence of slowing growth. \par \par \uc2  The market is likely to closely watch the U.S. June employment report due on Friday for clues on where the U.S. economy is heading. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht bounced sharply from a low of 45.70, its worst level since April 27, as talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred short covering. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bangkok said a major Japanese bank and a U.S. bank which often deal on behalf of the Bank of Thailand were seen selling dollars at around 45.60-65, fuelling speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was behind the move. \par \par \uc2  But assistant BOT governor Chettavee Chareonpitaks declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help support the baht, or on market talk it had been selling dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, he said the baht's fall was in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it was likely to fall further if the yen kept declining. \par \par \uc2  The baht had come under pressure from offshore sales after a senior BOT official said on Wednesday the bank would probably not require commercial banks to reveal the identities of offshore parties trading the baht, as planned earlier. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso kept a softer tone to end just above 53 having slipped to 5-= month lows of 53.10 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said a U.S. bank and a European bank sold around $15-20 million from 53.0 pesos, fanning talk they were acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They also reported talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had asked its auditors to carefully monitor transactions of at least eight local and foreign banks in Manila. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said most of the dollar buying was by importers and trading houses looking to hedge their requirements for the second half of 2001. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left key interest rates unchanged in a widely expected move. The overnight borrowing rate stands at 9.0 percent and the lending rate at 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Finance Secretary Jose Camacho said the peso's weakness was temporary. Economic Planning Secretary Dante Canlas said he expected inflation to rise to an annual 6.8 percent in July from 6.7 percent in June due to some volatility in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was dragged lower by a weaker yen and a bearish euro which are believed to be substantial components in Singapore's trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It dropped to an intraday low of 1.8260, and some believe it is just a matter of time before it retests 11-year lows of around 1.8270 touched on May 9. \par \par \uc2  The market awaits the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's review of monetary policy expected this month. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah drifted to 11,360 as sentiment was hurt by a weaker tone in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers spotted a state bank selling $2-3 million at 11,355 and 11,352, but the rupiah's upside was limited. \par \par \uc2  Senior IMF officials arrived in Indonesia on a mission aimed at reviving a stalled $5 billion loan programme. \par \par \uc2  The programme has been deadlocked for more than six months over Indonesia's foot-dragging on economic reforms and controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law amendments. The team is expected to remain in Jakarta for up to 10 days. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was easier in line with the yen but took the Bank of Korea's widely expected quarter percentage point interest rate easing in its stride. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its overnight call rate target to 4.75 percent after a cut of similar proportion in February. \par \par \uc2  With the cut already factored in, dealers said uncertainty over whether monetary easing would be followed by a weaker won policy kept players from taking aggressive positions. \par \par \uc2  Economists were divided over whether the BOK, caught between a sagging economy and inflation levels close to the bank's ceiling, would lower borrowing costs further in coming months. \par \par \uc2  The won was also cushioned by expected inflows in foreign investment, but concerns over the yen, a grim economic outlook and equity-related dollar demand capped the upside. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was weighed by the yen and as local stock market losses raised concerns foreign investors may convert the cash generated by recent selling to U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again active, capping the Taiwan dollar's fall at around 34.49, dealers in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices contracted for the second successive month. The June CPI shrank 0.16 percent on the year, after an 0.21 contraction in May. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said with little room left for further monetary easing, declining inflation would raise expectations Taiwan may ease its grip on the exchange rate to spur growth and exports. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0920 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.43\tab  124.91\tab    -0.41\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8253\tab  1.8243\tab    -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.465\tab  34.426\tab    -0.11\par  Korean won   1296.40\tab 1294.50\tab    -0.15\par  Baht\tab      45.46\tab   45.50\tab    +0.09\par  Peso\tab      52.85\tab   52.93\tab    +0.15\par  Rupiah\tab 11355.00     11350.00\tab    -0.04\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.43\tab  114.45\tab    -8.75\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8253\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.86\par  Taiwan dlr    34.465\tab  32.900\tab    -4.54\par  Korean won   1296.40\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.5