\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late, But Off Low; Tracks Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2001\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower against the U.S. dollar late Thursday, but off its intraday trough, as it tracked a weaker yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0832 GMT (4:32 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.8256, up from S$1.8243 late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.8244 and S$1.8263 Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose to near its 11-year high of S$1.8267 set on May 8 as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged to Y125.59. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that trading was fairly light, due to fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Such concerns emerged after the U.S. dollar broke key resistance at S$1.8250. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was unconfirmed talk that the MAS checked rates, but there were no signs of action by local banks and other banks that usually act on behalf of the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Local and U.S. banks were the most active buyers of U.S. dollars against the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the Singapore dollar may well retest its recent 11-year low against the U.S. dollar, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to drift higher overnight and over the next few days. \par \par \uc2  In overnight trading, support for the U.S. dollar is expected at S$1.8230, and resistance at S$1.8280, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \pa