\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late On Yen; Thin Trading, Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2001\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower late Wednesday, as it tracked a weaker yen in thin, range-bound trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0820 GMT the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8243, up from S$1.8212 late Tuesday. It traded between $1.8228 and S$1.8243. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar opened lower, in line with a weaker yen which came within striking range of the Y125 mark against the dollar but succeeded in staying above it. \par \par \uc2  Local banks were active buyers and sellers of U.S. dollars though the day, and some U.S. names were also seen buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Generally there was some buying on dips, but trade has basically been thin," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that market sentiment toward the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also hurt by talk that the Singapore government may cut its 3.5%-5.5% growth forecast for 2001 when it issues an advance estimate of growth in the second quarter on July 10. \par \par \uc2  Trading is expected to continue to remain light overnight with U.S. markets being closed for Independence Day. \par \par \uc2  Support for the U.S. dollar is expected around S$1.8230, with resistance at S$1.8250. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there will be any great attempt to take it higher," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The S$1.8250 resistance is expected to hold as market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at or above that level. \par \par \uc2  Prices of benchmark \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bonds ended mixed in a directionless market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market participants are looking to U.S. unemployment data, due Friday, for clues on whether the Federal Reserve will need to cut rates further. Also awaited is next week's issuance of Singapore second quarter growth data and an expected revision of the 2001 growth forecast, they added. \par \par \uc2  The yields on two- and five-year bonds were unchanged at 2.20% and 2.94%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was up one basis point at 3.33%, while the 10-year bond yield finished one basis point lower at 3.62%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web Site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps ended flat to a tad lower, in\par tandem with local bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, interest rates held mostly steady.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed one basis point down at\par 3.52%, while the 10-year swap offer also ended one basis point lower at\par 3.76%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swap offer was unchanged from\par Tuesday at 108 basis points.\par                  Late Wednesday       Late Tuesday\par                  bid      offer     bid     offer\par Overnight        1.8750%  2.0000%   1.8750%  2.0000%\par 3-Month          2.1250%  2.2500%   2.1250%  2.2500%\par 1-Year           2.2500%  2.3750%   2.2500%  2.3750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4802;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx74030ia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
