\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Easier on soft tankan, NAPM eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,095 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2001\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In SINGAPORE story headlined "Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Easier on soft \par \par \uc2   tankan, NAPM eyed" please read in paragraph 15 "The rupiah \par \par \uc2   stood above the key 11,400 mark..." instead of "The rupiah \par \par \uc2   stood above the key 14,000 mark..." (corrects the rupiah \par \par \uc2  level). \par \par \uc2  A corrected version follows. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 2 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicked off the the first trading session of the third quarter on Monday on a bearish note as the market watched out for economic data from their biggest export markets. \par \par \uc2  The yen dipped to around 125 to the dollar even though the Bank of Japan's tankan business sentiment survey came in pretty much in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  The main diffusion index for large manufacturers fell to minus 16. A Reuters survey had shown a median forecast of minus 16, with forecasts ranging from minus 11 to minus 25. \par \par \uc2  However, the fall in planned capital investment for business year 2001/02 was only 1.3 percent from the previous year and against a forecast of a 4.8 percent decline. That raised hopes of a possible recovery later in the year. \par \par \uc2  In the U.S., the key NAPM index for June is slated for 1400 GMT Monday and is expected to rise to 42.8 from 42.1 in May. \par \par \uc2  That would suggest a slower rate of decline of activity in a sector which comprises one-fifth of the overall economy, though a NAPM reading under 50 still indicates industrial activity is shrinking. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won eased in line with the yen, and as players preferred to stay long of the dollar ahead of a revised economic policy for the second half to be announced at 0300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers in Singapore said expected foreign investments and equity-related inflows were likely to underpin the downside, keeping the won within a near-term range of 1,290-1,310. \par \par \uc2  Hopes of investment inflows and fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the won in an uptrend channel against the dollar since it touched a low of 1,365.30 on April 4. \par \par \uc2  However, the upside is capped at around 1,280 due to concerns about the yen and a bleak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht hovered around the lower end of its recent 45.04-45.41 range as a weaker yen dragged down most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market was uninspired by key monthly data released on Friday. Although the economic numbers showed improvement in exports, analysts are not convinced that the worst is over. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the onshore market eased after the mid-year tax payment period had passed, indicating liquidity has returned to the market and it could be used to fund dollar holdings. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate was quoted at -4/-2 satang per dollar in the onshore market and 10/13 satang per dollar offshore. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah stood above the key 11,400 mark in a listless market as players took heart from a local press report that an IMF team will visit Indonesia at the end of this week to negotiate a new pact. \par \par \uc2  The report raised hope that a new pact would lead to resumption of the Fund's frozen $5 billion programme. The country desperately needs the Fund to release a $400 million loan delayed since last year to win investor and donor confidence. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected players to take some profits on the dollar because of the report, but the rupiah's upside was likely to be capped at 11,250 due to lingering political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar stumbled to seven-week lows of 1.8241 after some Australian banks bought the U.S. dollar due to a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did exist but some now reckon the absence of the authorities might mean they were tolerating the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weather the slowdown. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar is overbought against the Sing dollar, with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 73.97, indicating some scope for short-term correction. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso slid to 52.50, its lowest since January 19, weighed by the weaker yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Manila dealers said a European bank was defending the peso at 52.50, fueling talk it was acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Speculation was tense the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the peso through some foreign banks last week, but governor Rafael Buenaventura had repeatedly denied such rumours. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the peso would find a floor at around 52.70 as charts showed the dollar was heavily overbought with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 91.83. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Sunday the country's outstanding external debt had fallen four percent to $49.949 billion as of end-March from $52.06 billion from end-2000. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar eased at open but quickly pared most of its losses on expected equity-linked inflows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there were no signs of the usual aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far, which should encourage players to test levels beyond 34.50 later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar is in a downtrend against the U.S. dollar dating from May 21 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engineered its fall from a high of 32.91. \par \par \uc2  But since then, the bank has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly within 34.00-34.50 band, though Thursday's rate cut and poor economic data has triggered speculation it may allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle in a weaker band. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0141 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.63\tab  124.26\tab    -0.30\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8226\tab  1.8206\tab    -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.431\tab  34.435\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1298.00\tab 1299.90\tab    +0.15\par  Baht\tab      45.26\tab   45.28\tab    +0.04\par  Peso\tab      52.47\tab   52.35\tab    -0.23\par  Rupiah\tab 11370.00     11395.00\tab    +0.22\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.63\tab  114.45\tab    -8.17\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8226\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.72\par  Taiwan dlr    34.431\tab  32.900\tab    -4.45\par  Korean won   1298.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.62\par  Baht\tab      45.26\tab   43.70\tab    -3.45\par  Peso\tab      52.47\tab   50.75\tab    -3.28\par  Rupiah\tab 11370.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -16.71\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912d