\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Fed cut boon countered by yen softness. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,033 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2001\par 04:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drew little support from the Federal Reserve's 25-basis-point cut overnight as hopes for possible recovery in the U.S. were clouded by concerns over Japan's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market took the Fed's cut to mean that the easing cycle may be nearing an end, but it was pretty much in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  "This can be taken as good news, but I don't expect any big reactions from the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this time," said Syetarn Hansakul, economist at WestLB. \par \par \uc2  "At the end of the day, the market will look at how the cut would translate into the U.S. ability to take more exports from Asia. Our view is that we might very well be at the bottom, but when we are going to take off from here is a question. Japan's bleak economic picture will also limit the upside," she said. \par \par \uc2  The yen slipped to the wrong side of 124 following weaker-than-expected Japanese industrial data which showed a 1.2 percent month-on-month decline in May, compared with an average forecast of a fall of 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Players were cautious ahead of Bank of Japan's (BOJ) policy meeting later in the day amid speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to decide against easing its super-loose policy further. \par \par \uc2  The market will also watch out for Korea's May current account data due out at 0300 GMT and Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was stuck at around 1,300, wedged between exporter dollar offers and equity-linked dollar buying. Players warily eyed the yen ahead of the BOJ policy meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said players were also reluctant to take aggressive positions ahead of the May current account data due 0300 GMT. June consumer prices and May industrial output are due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were net sellers of local stocks worth about 140 billion won in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar slipped to 1.8230 from 1.8196 in thin morning trading, with some European and local banks looking to buy dollars at 1.8200. \par \par \uc2  The recent run of gloomy data reinforced view the economy was indeed weakening and fanned speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) would shift its monetary policy to neutral from tightening at its policy review in July. \par \par \uc2  But many analysts believe the current stance is neutral in reality. Dealers said the Sing dollar would retest 1.8267, 11-year lows hit on May 9 in the near future. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht weakened alongside the yen, hovering around 45.20 in a thin market as players braced for key monthly economic data due out on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But the downside was underpinned by foreign investment in local stocks and comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it aimed to keep the baht stable, indicating its willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both sides. \par \par \uc2  Onshore baht funding costs eased slightly as demand for funds ahead of mid-year tax payment subsided. The one-month forward rate dipped back into discounts at -2/1 satang per dollar. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was dragging its feet around 11,400 on political worries, but with few players interested in pulling it lower amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the rupiah would stay within a narrow range with the market focused on government efforts to appease the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  A renewed threat to impose emergency rule by President Abdurrahman Wahid has reignited worries over political stability but dealers said possible resumption of lending by the IMF could help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The government has indicated it was prepared to delay controversial changes to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws while the IMF said the move would result in resumption of talks with Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged down to 52.32 from 52.29 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said importers were keen to buy dollars from 52.20, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered support at around 52.50. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave interest rates unchanged when its monetary board meets later in the day, following the bank's comment it would keep them steady unless the Fed cuts by 100 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate stands at 9.0 percent and the lending rate at 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Jitters persisted after the military said late on Wednesday soldiers shot dead four Muslim rebels in the south but failed to locate any of more than 20 Filipino and U.S. hostages held by them for weeks. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar weakened, weighed by expected equity-linked U.S. dollar demand and ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly board meeting widely expected to track the Fed's move. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold a net 889.43 million Taiwan dollar worth of local stocks on Wednesday, and dealers in Singapore said the sale proceeds would be chasing U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Expected rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also sparked speculation it may allow the Taiwan dollar to ease into a weaker range of 34.50-35.00. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0137 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.35\tab  124.33\tab    -0.02\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8217\tab  1.8197\tab    -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.489\tab  34.456\tab    -0.10\par  Korean won   1301.20\tab 1298.80\tab    -0.18\par  Baht\tab      45.23\tab   45.20\tab    -0.07\par  Peso\tab      52.31\tab   52.29\tab    -0.04\par  Rupiah\tab 11415.00     11393.00\tab    -0.19\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.35\tab  114.45\tab    -7.96\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8217\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.68\par  Taiwan dlr    34.489\tab  32.900\tab    -4.61\par  Korean won   1301.20\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.86\par  Baht\tab      45.23\tab   43.70\tab    -3.38\par  Peso\tab      52.31\tab   50.75\tab    -2.98\par  Rupiah\tab 11415.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -17.04\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6s00t42\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
