\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Hostage to fickle yen, Argentina eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,110 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept an easier tone late Tuesday on uncertainty over the yen's near-term outlook, but weathered any fallout from Argentina's introduction of a special exchange rate for exporters and importers. \par \par \uc2  The yen recovered sharply from one-month lows against the dollar after Bank of Japan governor Masaru Hayami said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was needed if \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates move too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  Hayami also said Japan should not drive the yen lower because of its potential impact on neighbouring countries and given a surplus on Japan's current account. \par \par \uc2  The comment pushed the yen up to around 123.35 from around 123.60, but analysts said its outlook remained grim due to worries about Japan's faltering economy. \par \par \uc2  There was little reaction to Argentina's decision to expand its dollar peg to include the euro for exporters and importers, in a bid to make its goods cheaper for foreign buyers. \par \par \uc2  The move caused much confusion and a sell-off in Latin American markets on Monday on fears it would lead to a dismantling of Argentina's 1991 convertibility system, which is widely credited with bringing economic stability to the country. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso slid to five-month lows of 52.38 as corporates scrambled to buy the dollar on the weaker yen and concerns about the unsolved kidnapping problem in the southern Philippines. Manila dealers said players were still keen to buy the U.S. dollar, even with charts showing it was heavily overbought, unless the government resolved the hostage crisis. \par \par \uc2  "We'll take any excuse to buy the dollar. And we know the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't afford to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with their small reserves," a local bank dealer said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves stood at $14.44 billion at end-April. \par \par \uc2  But others said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might take the opportunity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the market was heavily long of dollars. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR The Sing dollar finally burst through the 1.8180 support, hitting five-week lows of 1.8194, following the fragile yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said U.S and European banks were aggressively buying the U.S. dollar in the afternoon, triggering stop-loss dollar orders at 1.8180. It later recovered some ground with the yen. \par \par \uc2  They expected prospects for a weaker yen to pressure the Sing dollar, with some dealers now doubting the authorities would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until it hits 1.8230-50, levels it has not seen since rebounding from 11-year lows of around 1.8270 in May. \par \par \uc2  It was pulled off those levels when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore sold U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, later confirming it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht held up well against the dollar, mostly due to higher funding costs offshore, which were driven by persistent fears of higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said despite reassurance from the authorities that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plan to increase interest rates soon, the market was not convinced. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, concerns over potential fallout from Argentina also jacked up baht funding costs on expectations demand to borrow the baht to buy the dollar could soon pick up. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market rose to 20/22 satang per dollar from around 8/10 satang late last week. The 12-month tenor edged up to 140/160 satangs. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  News of a bomb blast in Jakarta and another clash between police and students protesting fuel price hikes dragged the rupiah to a two-week low of 11,385 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Five people were wounded when a powerful bomb exploded at a boarding-house in a Jakarta suburb while police fired teargas to disperse 100 stone-throwing students near a university. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said dollar profit-taking by interbank players and some export-related inflows beyond 11,350 capped its downside. They said there was no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but players were cautious a test of 11,400 may invite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There was little immediate reaction to chief economic minister Burhanuddin Abdullah's comment that the government was willing to revise proposed changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, a key obstacle to releasing long-delayed IMF loans. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring the confusion on the economic front, the chief of the statistics bureau said price hikes in key sectors would push 2001 inflation above a revised budget target of 9.3 percent, approved only over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won tracked the yen lower, ending at 1,304.9 per dollar, its weakest close since May 16. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was also weighed by expected equity-linked outflows. Foreign investors, who were net sellers of local stocks for the third consecutive session, sold 172.1 billion won worth of shares on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off a remark by a senior official from a government think-tank calling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates in the second half of the year to boost the sagging economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its overnight call rate target steady at 5.0 percent for June, citing growing inflationary pressure. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was a shade off its session low of 34.43, weighed by equity-related outflows and pessimism over the economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's active presence in the market prompted some dollar profit-taking but overall sentiment was glum. The U.S. dollar was also looking overbought, with a 14-day relative strength index reading of 80.27. \par \par \uc2  May export orders, due on Friday, were expected to confirm the grim economic picture, with economists polled by Reuters predicting on average a 14.34 percent on-year decline after April's 6.63 percent drop. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0903 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.01\tab  123.36\tab    +0.28\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8178\tab  1.8166\tab    -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.403\tab  34.379\tab    -0.07\par  Korean won   1300.00\tab 1297.00\tab    -0.23\par  Baht\tab      45.26\tab   45.32\tab    +0.13\par  Peso\tab      52.29\tab   51.98\tab    -0.60\par  Rupiah\tab 11370.00     11280.00\tab    -0.79\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.01\tab  114.45\tab    -6.96\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8178\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.47\par  Taiwan dlr    34.403\tab  32.900\tab    -4.37\par  Korean won   1300.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.77\par  Baht\tab      45.26\tab   43.70\tab    -3.45\par  Peso\tab      52.29\tab   50.75\tab    -2.95\par  Rupiah\tab 11370.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -16.71\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6j01ftr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
