\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen weighs, market eyes Argentina. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,097 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 03:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retained their bearish tone in early trade on Tuesday as the yen languished near one-month lows and the market eyed the potential impact of Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan on emerging Asia. \par \par \uc2  The yen , which is tracked closely by most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slid to 123.52 overnight after the Bank of Japan's monthly report said the slowdown in the economy was intensifying. \par \par \uc2  It recouped some lost ground after Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Tuesday he thought the overnight moves in dollar/yen were "quite big", adding however, that he could only monitor them for now. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's decision to introduce a special exchange rate for exporters and importers, by expanding its dollar peg to include the euro, was also being warily eyed after it sparked much confusion and a sell-off on Latin American markets overnight. \par \par \uc2  Investors fear the move could be a step toward dismantling Argentina's 1991 convertibility system which pegs the peso to the U.S. dollar and is widely credited with bringing economic stability to the country. \par \par \uc2  But analysts expected the impact on Asia to be limited and mainly psychological, with Philippine sovereign bonds looking the most vulnerable due to their significant weighting in the JP Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus (EMBI-Plus). \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, local factors offered little support to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the Philippines' January-April trade surplus shrinking as both exports and imports declined. This followed Monday's news that Singapore's non-oil domestic exports for May fell a nominal 9.0 percent year-on-year, worse than the market's consensus of around a six percent decline. \par \par \uc2  And political uncertainty continued to plague Indonesia, the Philippines and Thailand. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar was on the defensive at 1.8160 due to the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  It has avoided a break of 1.8180 thanks largely to dollar sales of around $100 million by a European bank late on Monday, stirring talk the orders may be linked to an M&A deal. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment for the Sing dollar soured after weaker-than-expected non-oil exports data for May, which raised risks of a technical recession for the trade-driven economy. \par \par \uc2  They said European banks were keen to push dollar/Sing above 1.8180, a level it has failed to break for the past five sessions on fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last month when the local dollar hit 11-year lows of around 1.8270. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso floundered to fresh six-month lows of 52.22 on concerns about possible spillover damage on emerging markets from Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan. \par \par \uc2  The country has a significant weighting in the EMBI-Plus, which widened 25 basis points to 758 basis points late on Monday, representing the heightened risk. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said the unsolved kidnapping saga in the southern Philippines and the weaker yen also added to the gloom, but they expected fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso above 52.50. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was trapped in a tug-of-war between a weaker yen and confusion over \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players were cautious after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not abandoned plans to tighten disclosure rules, but it just needed more time to work out how to do it. \par \par \uc2  Some investors also kept a low profile ahead of a verdict on Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's graft case, which is expected by August. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Thaksin made an emotional 20-minute speech to the Constitutional Court to defend himself against charges he deliberately concealed assets. He denies wrongdoing, but if found guilty would be banned from politics for five years. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was a shade above the 11,300 level amid worries Monday's transport strikes against last week's 30 percent hike in fuel prices may spread to other cities after some regional authorities raised bus fares. \par \par \uc2  The strikes were mostly peaceful apart from some clashes between students and police in Jakarta in which several protestors were injured. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players feared the protests may get more violent, but the rupiah might remain relatively insulated as most interbank players were showing little trading interest and dollar-starved local corporates were also keeping a low profile. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was hurt by a weaker yen and expected equity-linked outflows after foreign investors sold a net 232 billion won worth of local shares in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  But its downside was cushioned by hopes of inflows from Hynix Semiconductor's $1.25 billion global depository receipts issue. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea said the debt default ratio fell to 0.21 percent in May from 0.28 percent in April due to reduced fallout from bankrupt Daewoo Group companies and Samsung Motors. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty about the yen's near-term direction and the Nasdaq's overnight fall to six-month lows were expected to keep the Taiwan dollar under pressure. \par \par \uc2  The local stock market is already reeling from first quarter profit warnings from electronics companies at home which have triggered net selling by foreign equity investors. \par \par \uc2  However, some profit-taking was possible on U.S. dollar longs, as charts showed an overbought U.S. dollar with the 14-day relative strength index reading at 79.17. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar has been in a downtrend against the U.S. dollar since May 21 when it slipped from a high of 32.91. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts believe the decline was engineered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the island's sagging exports. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0149 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.11\tab  121.37\tab    -1.41\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8146\tab  1.8105\tab    -0.23\par  Taiwan dlr    34.378\tab  34.379\tab    +0.00\par  Korean won   1299.00\tab 1291.00\tab    -0.62\par  Baht\tab      45.30\tab   45.27\tab    -0.07\par  Peso\tab      52.28\tab   51.98\tab    -0.58\par  Rupiah\tab 11290.00     11250.00\tab    -0.35\par  Ringgit\tab  3.8000\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.11\tab  114.45\tab    -7.03\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8146\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.30\par  Taiwan dlr    34.378\tab  32.900\tab    -4.30\par  Korean won   1299.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.69\par  Baht\tab      45.30\tab   43.70\tab    -3.53\par  Peso\tab