\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen rebound provides relief. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,046 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2001\par 04:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 15 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly steadier in early trade on Friday as the yen recouped some lost ground after U.S. manufacturers called for the government to relax its strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected market activity to be subdued ahead of the U.S. consumer price data due out at 1230 GMT for clues on what the Federal Reserve policy makers might do when they meet on June 26-27 to decide on the direction of interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were also reluctant to move aggressively before the Bank of Japan completes its two-day policy meeting on Friday. Political pressure has been building on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to further loosen its already ultra loose monetary policy following data showing the economy had unexpectedly shrunk 0.2 percent in the first three months of this year. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. data continues to show weakness in the U.S. economy and thus for global growth prospects. Moreover, the yen looks set now to weaken further towards 130 against the dollar," Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg, said in a daily note on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "As such, we remain bearish on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and out long term targets remain 35.00 for the Taiwan dollar, 1400 for the Korean won, 47.00 for the Thai baht and 1.8500 for the Singapore dollar," he said. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR The Taiwan dollar was at 34.39, within striking distance from 34.50, 32-month lows hit on May 28. \par \par \uc2  Gloomy prospects of the domestic economy has put the Taiwan dollar under pressure from offshore selling, triggered by a CSFB report earlier this week which forecast it to fall to 35.5-36 in three months. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg said in a research note the Taiwan dollar might fall to 35 in the long term once the next target of 34.5 is broken. SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar edged up to 1.8138 in listless morning trading from 1.8157 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said speculators including U.S. funds liquidated their long dollar positions following the firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  But they added many players were keen to buy the U.S. dollar on dips at 1.8130 to take profits at 1.8180, level the market fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht moved in a narrow range amid political uncertainty as the market watched political development ahead of Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's graft trial on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin, who was elected at a landslide in January, is being tried by the Constitutional Court for failing to declare all this wealth when he was a minister in 1990s. He denied any wrongdoing. If found guilty, he can be banned from politics for five years. \par \par \uc2  The trial will be concluded on Monday but the verdict might be delivered in July or August. \par \par \uc2  Pressure groups have organised political rallies in various form to support him, and press for an acquittal. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said if the court stuck solely to the question of whether he deliberately concealed his wealth, Thaksin's chance of survival would be slim. \par \par \uc2  But if the judges brought into consideration the public sentiment, he is likely to be acquitted. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won opened a touch firmer, drawing support from a steadier yen and expected inflows. \par \par \uc2  Momentum should be sustained on if Hynix Semiconductor is successful with its planned $1.25 billion global share offering. \par \par \uc2  But its upside is likely to be capped by Nasdaq-inspired losses in the local stocks and doubts over the country's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  The one-month won on the non-deliverable forward market was quoted at 1294.7/1295.6, and the six-month at 1304/1306. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was expected to stay within a narrow 51.20-51.60 range, with gains in the yen and a steadier baht supporting the downside, and dollar bids by corporates and importers capping the upside. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the underlying sentiment was bearish on the peso given the kidnapping crisis and the recent downgrade of growth estimates by the government. \par \par \uc2  But a lack of fresh leads and with charts showing the dollar overbought, most players were seeking to book profits on dollar gains. \par \par \uc2  The 14-day relative strength index (RSI) showed a reading of 77.61 for dollar/peso last seen in late April when the pair rose from a low of 50.25 to touch a high of 51.45 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was little moved from its tight range around the 11,250 mark with trading interest minimal on a lack of any major development on the political front. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said steadier regionals may limit the downside but the rupiah was unlikely to stray far from the current 11,200-11,350 range. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah is simply simmering down. No one seem to be interested in it any more. Maybe a major political event will provoke some trading interest," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said most players in the market have squared their positions in anticipation of an early and peaceful exit of embattled President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  "But nothing is happening and its not clear if things will turn out the way market wants them to," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0207 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.46\tab  122.11\tab    +0.54\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8126\tab  1.8157\tab    +0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    34.440\tab  34.395\tab    -0.13\par  Korean won   1291.00\tab 1287.00\tab    -0.31\par  Baht\tab      45.28\tab   45.34\tab    +0.13\par  Peso\tab      51.47\tab   51.34\tab    -0.24\par  Rupiah\tab 11242.00     11245.00\tab    +0.03\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.46\tab  114.45\tab    -5.77\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8126\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.440\tab  32.900\tab    -4.47\par  Korean won   1291.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.08\par  Baht\tab      45.28\tab   43.70\tab    -3.49\par  Peso\tab      51.47\tab   50.75\tab    -1.39\par  Rupiah\tab 11242.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -15.76\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6f01kgj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
