\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late; Tracks Weaker Yen, Regionals \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2001\par 11:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower late Wednesday, in line with Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of continued weakness in the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0916 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.8160, up from S$1.8146 late Tuesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.8158 and S$1.8180. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the U.S. dollar's rise above Y122 hurt the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, U.S. dollar gains were capped at S$1.8180 as companies sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A local bank that had been buying U.S. dollars in the morning turned seller as it was caught long after companies sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via several foreign banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's retreat from S$1.8160 also reflected its decline from Y122.40 to around Y122.10. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the U.S. dollar to remain capped at S$1.8200 overnight, with support at S$1.8130. \par \par \uc2  Prices of benchmark Singapore government bonds ended slightly lower as banks trimmed their positions, particularly in longer-dated bonds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Interest rate swaps were narrowly mixed, with most swaps edging higher due to a weaker Singapore dollar and higher bond yields. \par \par \uc2  In the interbank money market, term interest rates remained steady, while the overnight rose slightly above 2% amid increased demand for funds. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two- and five-year bonds ended one basis point higher each at 2.28% and 2.95%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yields on the seven-year bonds also finished two basis points higher at 2.32%, while the yield on the 10-year paper rose one basis point to 3.56%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web Site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed one basis point higher at\par 3.53%, while the 10-year swap offer fell one basis point to 3.73%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swap offer narrowed to 104\par basis points from 106 basis points Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  Late Wednesday     Late Tuesday\par                  bid      offer     bid     offer\par Overnight        2.0000%  2.1250%   1.5000%  1.6250%\par 3 Month          2.1250%  2.2500%   2.1250%  2.2500%\par 1 Year           2.2500%  2.3750%   2.2500%  2.3750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 421-4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6d02par\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
