\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rangebound on uncertainty in majors. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,087 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2001\par 10:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bobbed within their recent ranges on Friday as players held back from taking aggressive positions amid uncertainty about the direction of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and thin weekend conditions. \par \par \uc2  However, given the unabated flow of poor economic numbers and more deterioration expected in the second quarter, most players were keen to buy the dollar on dips with no fresh domestic leads to make them think twice. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand failed to stir the market when it raised its key 14-day repo rate by a full percentage point to 2.5 percent. Markets had been expecting higher rates since the sacking of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief last week over his insistence on a low rate regime. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked after two foreign banks, usually active on its behalf, were spotted buying upto $40 million earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The tech-sensitive won and Taiwan dollar were broadly steady following overnight rises in U.S. tech and semiconductor indices. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was helped by recent gains in the yen and euro , following losses in sterling . \par \par \uc2  The pound stumbled to 15-year lows for the third day as traders bet a victorious Labour Party would push for Britain's early entry into the euro. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was stuck at around 45.10 amid speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to raise its key interest rate may be followed by fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbs to stem capital outflows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rate hike in itself was too small to have an impact on the capital flight estimated at $2.36 billion in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Thai officials have repeatedly denied plans to impose capital controls or to enforce postponed reporting requirements soon. \par \par \uc2  Contradictory comments induced more confusion with Finance Minister Somkid Jatsuripitak saying the rate hike would encourage banks to lend more and attract more deposits while Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said rates were still too low to have impact. \par \par \uc2  Fears of new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosure rules, fresh restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade and higher rates have kept the baht firm against the dollar since it touched a low of 45.85 on April 9. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday when the baht hit a high of 44.68 has made players wary of testing the upside. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hugged an 11,200 session low on local corporate demand for the dollar which prompted interbank players to book profits on the rupiah's recent gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the political situation was still tense with players cautious amid rumours President Abdurrahman Wahid would sack the military chief. \par \par \uc2  But speculation Wahid may quit peacefully had also not died. Those rumours have helped the rupiah gain ground against the dollar from a low of 12,215 touched on April 26. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso slipped to hit a low of 50.96 despite denial by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  it was in the market buying dollars to boost its reserves or for foreign debt repayment needs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said two foreign banks that were executing the dollar purchases were usually active on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the amount, estimated at $30-40 million, was too big to be associated with a corporate client. \par \par \uc2  However, some interbank players were seen booking profits on the dollar's gains from around 50.90 while corporates and importers kept to the sidelines for most of the day. SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was confined to a well-worn 1.8060-1.8110 range amid a dearth of new leads and no fresh corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  Narrowing price action in the dollar/Sing has led to the formation of a constricting triangle on the weekly chart following the dollar's steep month-long rise from March 4. \par \par \uc2  While the charts suggest an upside break for the U.S. dollar, dealers said wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cushion any falls towards 1.82. \par \par \uc2  The MAS sold the U.S. dollar heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last month, even admitting it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when the Sing dollar looked set to slide further after hitting new 11-year lows near 1.8270. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won gained from a robust 3.4 percent bounce in local stocks as chips and financials rallied on an improved outlook for the semiconductor business and signs of progress on corporate reform. Korea's semiconductor exports make up about 10 percent of GDP and a third of total exports. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net 221.1 billion won worth of shares on the Korean stock market on Friday after selling a net 26.8 billion in the past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  But importer dollar demand capped the won's gains at 1,283.1 for the day. \par \par \uc2  Despite its two-month-old firming trend on rising hopes of foreign direct investment inflows, the won has had trouble sustaining a rise above the 1,283 level, which marks the 62 percent retracement of the dollar's February 21-April 4 rally. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was a shade higher from late Thursday levels as the local stock market tracked gains in U.S. technology and semiconductor indices overnight. \par \par \uc2  The 1.42 percent rise in the benchmark TAIEX raised hopes of fresh foreign equity-linked inflows. \par \par \uc2  However, recent poor economic data and parliament's failure to approve key financial reforms kept sentiment depressed. \par \par \uc2  And with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen active on both sides, trading interest was also quite low. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0837 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.51\tab  119.93\tab    -0.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8080\tab  1.8100\tab    +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.053\tab  34.065\tab    +0.04\par  Korean won   1286.50\tab 1287.50\tab    +0.08\par  Baht\tab      45.12\tab   45.04\tab    -0.18\par  Peso\tab      50.90\tab   50.71\tab    -0.37\par  Rupiah\tab 11200.00     11140.00\tab    -0.54\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.51\tab  114.45\tab    -5.03\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8080\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.95\par  Taiwan dlr    34.053\tab  32.900\tab    -3.39\par  Korean won   1286.50\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.74\par  Baht\tab      45.12\tab   43.70\tab    -3.15\par  P