\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Docile in ranges but firm yen helps. \b0\par\par\uc2 978 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2001\par 03:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 7 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  idled around recent ranges early Thursday while the market pondered over two major driving factors at the moment, the yen and baht. \par \par \uc2  The yen firmed against the dollar as it made gains against sterling. The pound was struggling ahead of the British general election amid talk a Labour government would adopt the euro but at the same time engineer a much competitive exchange rate before conversion. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's gains were relatively minute, and analysts expect it to flag given the stagnant Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also been tracking the Thai baht, which was steady after it veered from a high of 44.74 to a low of 45.31 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand threw another curve ball at the market, which had been bailing out of dollar longs given uncertainty over new reporting rules and fears of higher interest rates and possible new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would delay the implementation of the rules, and Bangkok and Singapore dealers said there was talk the bank was buying dollars to cap the baht's rapid gains and bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. That spurred players to cover their short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank's change of heart added more confusion and was another blow to foreign investor confidence. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was stabilising above 45.30 in a market that was growing increasingly wary of the Bank of Thailand. \par \par \uc2  New \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting rules and worries over possible new restrictions and higher interest rates had driven the baht to a high of 44.74 on Wednesday, its best level since March 30. \par \par \uc2  But talk that the BOT had bought dollar at 44.80 and the bank's decision to delay the implementation of the new reporting rules sent the baht past 45 again late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore and Hong Kong dealers said players were uncomfortable with pushing the dollar/baht past Wednesday's high of 45.31. \par \par \uc2  But they added the baht was well-supported around 45, given local corporate dollar demand and the rumours of BOT \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  trailed after the firmer yen, but kept with a thin range of 1.8115-1.8120 as the market rooted around for fresh trading cues. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing was seen drifting around 1.8100, with some local players buying dollar on dips towards that level. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar/Sing's gains were limited to around 1.8130/40, close to the intraday highs on Tuesday and Wednesday, as U.S. names were spotted selling dollar around that level. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was expected to stay within its recent 50.50-50.80 range amid wariness over kidnappings by Muslim rebels and on rising local corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  A steady yen and the baht were likely to limit losses. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary board was also expected to lower key overnight interest rates after a slower than expected rise in May consumer prices index. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate is now at 9.0 percent and lending rate is at 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said a 50 basis point cut has already been priced in. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won dipped as trade resumed after the Memorial Day holiday on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said sentiment was glum on overnight profit warnings by J.P. Morgan Chase & Co and Hewlett-Packard Co and ahead of a preliminary report on quarterly earnings by computer giant Intel Corp due later in the day. \par \par \uc2  But they added the firmer yen was likely to lend support. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea was widely expected to hold its key overnight call rate at five percent on inflation concerns at its monthly policy meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged down on expected losses at the local stock market in line with the Nasdaq's fall overnight. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said further depressing the sentiment was the opposition-dominated parliament's failure to approve key financial reform bills. \par \par \uc2  However, with some help from the yen on the downside and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on guard on both sides, the Taiwan dollar was not expected to stray far from its recent 33.95-34.10 range. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hovered above 11,200 thanks to the relative quiet on Jakarta's turbulent political scene. \par \par \uc2  But the rupiah's gains were expected to be capped around the 11,000 level given strong local corporate dollar demand and caution ahead of a special impeachment session in August. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been creeping higher this week on hopes President Abdurrahman Wahid will be forced out of office without much violence. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts say while the rupiah is expected to spike higher with Wahid's probable departure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would later come under pressure given Indonesia's limping economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0125 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.24\tab  120.50\tab    +0.22\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8126\tab  1.8117\tab    -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr     34.08\tab   34.07\tab    -0.04\par  Korean won   1285.00\tab 1286.00\tab    +0.08\par  Baht\tab      45.32\tab   45.18\tab    -0.31\par  Peso\tab      50.76\tab   50.70\tab    -0.12\par  Rupiah\tab 11130.00     11185.00\tab    +0.49\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.24\tab  114.45\tab    -4.82\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8126\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.20\par  Taiwan dlr     34.02\tab   32.90\tab    -3.29\par  Korean won   1285.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.62\par  Baht\tab      45.32\tab   43.70\tab    -3.57\par  Peso\tab      50.76\tab   50.75\tab    -0.02\par  Rupiah\tab 11130.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -14.91\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6702ari\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
