\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady on local factors, eye on yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,011 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2001\par 03:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 6 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  steered a steady course early Wednesday thanks to local factors, though they were mindful of the yen's direction. \par \par \uc2  So far, domestic cues have played out to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' advantage. The Indonesian rupiah kept its firmer tone as the market hoped President Abdurrahman Wahid would soon be ousted. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, comments by the new Bank of Thailand governor Pridiyathorn Devakula, which indicated that interest rates would rise, boosted the baht. \par \par \uc2  But the yen slipped slightly against the dollar in overnight trading, and any further falls could dent regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Recent U.S. data also showed continued weakness in the economy, with productivity falling, labour costs rising and activity slowing in the manufacturing and service sectors. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said one of the conditions needed for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen was a recovery in the U.S. economy, which has yet to show itself. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Seoul were closed for a public holiday and will re-open on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was firmer despite the softer yen, extending gains to 44.80, its highest level since March 30. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said U.S. names and offshore banks began buying the baht late Tuesday on speculation of tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules effective on July 2 and expectations of higher rates. That triggered stop-loss dollar selling at 45.30, pushing the baht above 45. \par \par \uc2  But charts showed the dollar/baht was heavily overbought, with a 14-day relative strength index reading at 17.23, suggesting room for correction. \par \par \uc2  The cabinet formally approved a plan to establish a state-run Thai Asset Management Corp (TAMC) to buy bad loans from banks, which also gave the baht a marginal boost. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministry officials have said they expected TAMC to buy up to 1.35 trillion baht worth of non-performing loans from banks, of which about 1.1 trillion would come from state-owned or nationalised banks. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said the total NPLs in the Thai financial system stood at 17.6 percent of total loans. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar bobbed around 1.8110-1.8120, caught between a softer yen and recent gains in the baht and the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Analysts believe given the restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading environment in Thailand and Indonesia, players were using the Sing dollar as a proxy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing's upside was capped around 1.8100 on dollar buying by local corporates and the downside was around 1.8140 where hedge funds and local banks were seen selling the dollar earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts see 1.8200 as a strong near-term support on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso drifted around 50.50 with some peso selling interest given the baht's recent gains and ahead of the weekly policy meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary board on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said the market was also keeping an eye on developments on the political front. \par \par \uc2  President Gloria Arroyo said on Tuesday she was considering imposing martial law in the troubled southern island of Basilan where Muslim rebels are holed in with U.S. and Filipino hostages. \par \par \uc2  A slower than expected rise in the May consumer price index has raised expectations of further monetary easing with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying overnight rates may fall to 8.25 percent if annual inflation averages around 6.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate is now at 9.0 percent and lending rate is at 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was flat in light offshore trade as Seoul markets were closed for the Memorial Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been tracking the yen closely, though it could feel downward pressure from foreign investors' net sales of 107.6 billion won worth of local stocks on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won was at 1,293/95 and the six-month was at 1,302/05. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected another rangebound day for the Taiwan dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its recent range. The bank was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 34.02 and 34.14 in the past few days. \par \par \uc2  It opened a touch firmer at 34.037 against Tuesday's close of 34.043, but later slipped alongside the yen. \par \par \uc2  However, it was expected to be underpinned by fund inflows to the local stock market after the government announced stimulus measures on Monday to support the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net T$1.27 billion in shares on Tuesday, accumulating a net T$2.76 billion over the last four sessions. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah held onto its recent gains, with sentiment improving ahead of a special impeachment session in August. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said players were optimistic that President Abdurrahman Wahid would soon be kicked out of office. Parliament has censured him twice on charges of corruption and incompetency. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the rupiah's gains were limited due to Jakarta's mercurial political scene and the threat of violence from Wahid's more fanatical supporters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.31\tab  119.51\tab    -0.66\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8088\tab  1.8114\tab    +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.086\tab  34.043\tab    -0.13\par  Korean won   1286.00\tab 1284.00\tab    -0.16\par  Baht\tab      44.77\tab   45.07\tab    +0.67\par  Peso\tab      50.55\tab   50.55\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab 11125.00     11220.00\tab    +0.85\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.31\tab  114.45\tab    -4.87\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8088\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.00\par  Taiwan dlr    34.086\tab  32.900\tab    -3.48\par  Korean won   1286.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.70\par  Baht\tab      44.77\tab   43.70\tab    -2.39\par  Peso\tab      50.55\tab   50.75\tab    +0.40\par  Rupiah\tab 11125.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -14.88\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6602hc6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
