\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rangebound despite jumpy yen and baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,059 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2001\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 6 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted for the safety of their recent ranges on Wednesday as the yen and Thai baht see-sawed. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht fluctated from a high of 44.74 to back past the 45 mark amid speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars in order to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise and shore up reserves. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand declined to comment on the talk. It also said it would delay the implementation of new disclosure laws, adding to the uncertainty that had helped support the baht along with fears of new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, and higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers took a dour view on the latest developments in Thailand, saying they feared the offshore baht market was seeing its last days. \par \par \uc2  "If they (BOT) keep messing around, then it's going to go the way of Indonesia, where everyone had enough of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changing its mind and just got out," said a European bank dealer. Meanwhile, the yen slipped on renewed concerns over the stagnant Japanese economy and a firmer euro. \par \par \uc2  Seoul markets were closed for a public holiday and will re-open on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was on the backfoot as players rushed to cover their short dollar positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would delay new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade reporting rules, which were set for July 2. \par \par \uc2  After hitting a 44.74 high, its best level since March 30, the baht slipped past the 45 level again to hit a low of 45.31. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said there was speculation the Bank of Thailand was buying dollar around 44.80 in order to slow the baht's rise and build up its reserves. The bank later declined to comment on the talk. \par \par \uc2  But dealers saw the dollar's rally as short-lived given the uncertainty over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible new regulations and higher interest rates, and confusion over the new reporting rules have sent the baht higher as offshore players bailed out of dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar settled at 1.8120 after a volatile session saw it slip to 1.8130 from 1.8070 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The main catalyst was the dollar/baht, with dealers reporting U.S. funds buying back dollar/Sing from 1.8070. \par \par \uc2  A survey of economists by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore showed the country's economy is expected to grow 3.5 percent, at the lower end of the government's revised official forecast of 3.5 to 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  It also showed the weakness in the Sing dollar was likely to persist this year but the median exchange rate stood at 1.8000. Respondents expected the median exchange rate to strengthen to 1.770 in 2002. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar has lost more than four percent since the beginning of the year when it was at 1.7365. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso erased gains to slip to 50.72 from 50.50 earlier against 50.59 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said a local bank alone bought $20-30 million at 50.55-65 on behalf of corporates. A foreign bank was also spotted buying $5-10 million at 50.55. \par \par \uc2  They added investors were still cautious as Muslim rebels holding hostages in the southern Philippines said a U.S. missionary captive had been injured in clashes with troops. \par \par \uc2  Such concerns pushed stocks down for the third straight session, also bruising sentiment for the peso. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said hopes for a rate cut given benign inflation data earlier this week underpinned the peso at 50.80. \par \par \uc2  The policy-making Monetary Board meets on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate stands at 9.0 percent and the lending rate at 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged up to a session high of 11,120 before heavy local corporate dollar demand pulled it to levels around 11,200. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said the rupiah had been gaining on speculation President Abdurrahman Wahid may step down peacefully before impeachment hearings in August. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is expected to spike higher if Wahid resigns but analysts say any gains would be temporary given the country's poor economic conditions. \par \par \uc2  Moody's said the political and social turmoil eroding government's ability to implement economic policy were not limited to events surrounding the presidency. \par \par \uc2  However, it kept a stable outlook on its B3 foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  country ceiling for bonds and notes. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slipped by a hair's breadth due to the softer yen, but kept within a tidy range of 33.940-34.090. \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the Taiwan dollar from straying too far. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the bank has been spotted on both sides of the market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a tight range. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was stable in dozy offshore trade as Seoul markets were closed for a public holiday, and will re-open on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea will hold its monthly monetary policy setting meeting on Thursday. A recent Reuters poll showed economists unanimously seeing the bank holding its overnight call rate steady at five percent due to inflation fears. \par \par \uc2  On the offshore non-deliverable market, the one-month won was at 1,289/90 against 1,293/95 earlier in the day and the six-month was at 1,298/1,300 against 1,302/1,305. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.46\tab  119.51\tab    -0.79\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8120\tab  1.8114\tab    -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.065\tab  34.043\tab    -0.06\par  Korean won   1286.00\tab 1284.00\tab    -0.16\par  Baht\tab      45.20\tab   45.07\tab    -0.29\par  Peso\tab      50.70\tab   50.55\tab    -0.30\par  Rupiah\tab 11185.00     11220.00\tab    +0.31\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.46\tab  114.45\tab    -4.99\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8120\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.17\par  Taiwan dlr    34.065\tab  32.900\tab    -3.42\par  Korean won   1286.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.70\par  Baht\tab      45.20\tab   43.70\tab    -3.32\par  Peso\tab      50.70\tab   50.75\tab    +0.10\par  Rupiah\tab 11185.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -15.33\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6602cd4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
