\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Unsteady, but still rangebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,046 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2001\par 04:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 21 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  unsteady early Monday due to lingering unease over the Morgan \par \par \uc2  Stanley Capital International reweighting of its indices. \par \par \uc2      But analysts said the reweighting would have a limited \par \par \uc2  impact on markets as it had been largely priced in already. \par \par \uc2  They noted the announcement made on Saturday had few surprises. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was flat against the yen\tab   in early Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade, providing some relief for regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also little changed against the euro , which hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five-month lows on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With few fresh factors in sight, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to stay fenced in their recent ranges. Analysts say\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian markets were now looking for further clues as to where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economy of the United States, its largest export market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was headed in the second half.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the meantime, there was some major economic data from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the region due later in the week. Taiwan will issue its first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter current account data on Monday, April industrial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par production, export data and jobless rate on Wednesday, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first quarter gross domestic growth on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Korea is expected to issue first-quarter GDP on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar dipped more than a half cent to 1.8125 from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Friday's 1.8057, pressured by the lower yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said players took profits on short dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions, but the Sing's downside was supported by U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment banks actively selling the dollar at 1.8120.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's weighting in the MSCI's All Country World Free\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Index fell to 0.26 percent from 0.38 percent, but the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has shown little reaction as the move was well flagged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said fears of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were still intact, especially\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at levels above 1.8150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht drifted off to 45.60 from 45.42 late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bangkok dealers said Singapore-based banks bought the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar from 45.40, but rice exporters were offering the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 45.55.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They added local companies were keen to buy the baht at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below 45.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Thailand said late on Friday it did not expect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a decision by the government to raise its planned 2001/2002\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budget deficit would create debt financing problems for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government approved a plan to raise the budget deficit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 3.5 percent of GDP from 2.7 percent planned earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso also edged down in line with weaker regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , opening at 50.40 against 50.33 late on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Manila dealers expected companies with dollar debt are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking to buy the dollar from 50.20-30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance undersecretary Juanita Amatong said the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plans to sell between $500 million and $700 million worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bonds in the United States, Japan and Europe next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The National Treasurer said the foreign borrowing would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a crucial part of the government's mid-year financing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par programme. The country expects its budget deficit to reach 145\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion pesos this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Political uncertainty also weighed on the peso. Unofficial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par results showed President Gloria Arroyo's coalition was holding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its lead in the fight for 13 senate seats.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts have said Arroyo's coalition must win nine of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contested Senate seats to secure a majority and ensure passage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of vital economic reform measures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was flat as it trotted alongside the yen, though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment towards the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be lifted by cheer in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local bourse over MSCI's higher weighting for Korean shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts said any real gains from the MSCI reweighting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would be slight as it had been long anticipated, and fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign fund inflows due to the higher weighting would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par staggered. Korea's weighting rose by 3.3 percent in the MSCI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerging market index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, with little new in the market, the won was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely to break its recent range. Since May 7, it has kept\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within a narrow range of 1,294-1,310.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah succumbed to familiar complaints of thin dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity and local corporate dollar demand amid political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wrangling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was straddling the 11,400 mark, with little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relief in sigh as the country's political crisis dragged on.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest political scuttlebutt over the weekend in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta was that President Abdurrahman Wahid planned to declare\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a state of emergency in order to repel a bid to impeach him.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, a spokesman later denied Wahid would take such a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par measure. A cabinet meeting was also held on Sunday, with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two main players of the current political drama conspicuously\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par absent - Wahid and his deputy and political rival, Megawati\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sukarnoputri.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar drooped past 33 against Friday's close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 32.948 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was upset by a forecast from a research house\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that saw the local dollar at 38 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts have said they expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given Taiwan's slowing economy and heightened export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competition. However, most analysts do not see the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar falling past 35 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Taipei dealers said they spotted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling dollars in order to prevent steeper falls in the local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hopes for foreign fund inflows and exporters' dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were also expected to underpin the local dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0147\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.40\tab  123.23\tab    -0.14\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8110\tab  1.8078\tab    -0.18\par  Taiwan dlr     33.11\tab   32.95\tab    -0.49\par  Korean won   1303.90