\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Aided by steady yen, U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2001\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 18 (Reuters) - A steady yen continued to provide support to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Friday and further help was expected from encouraging U.S. data and Wall Street's overnight performance. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the yen was off overnight highs but far from lows around 124 seen earlier in the week, aided by option plays, recent gains in the Nikkei, and doubts over Japan's tolerance for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But analysts warned speculation on the impact of changes to the MSCI equity indices on Saturday could result in outflow of funds from Japanese stocks in favour of U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  A surprise fall in U.S. first-time jobless claims to their lowest level in two months buoyed hopes of a recovery in export-dependent Asia's largest market. \par \par \uc2  The weekly claims fell by 8,000 to 380,000, signalling resilience of the labour market - keenly watched by analysts for its links to consumer spending which accounts for two-thirds of overall economic activity in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq rose 1.26 percent and the Dow 0.29 percent as computer giant Hewlett-Packard reported a quarterly profit higher than market estimates. \par \par \uc2  Markets will now watch for any clues from Fed chairman Alan Greenspan's speech to bankers later Friday and to an economic club on May 24. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, no surprises were expected from the second day of the Bank of Japan's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar kept a firmer tone at just above 1.8050, showing little reaction to news gross domestic product rose 4.5 percent on year in the first quarter, a shade below the government's advance estimate of 4.6 percent growth. On an annualised seasonally adjusted quarter-on-quarter basis, first quarter growth was down a sharp 11 percent against a 10 percent growth rate in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  The Ministry of Trade and Industry said the second quarter would weaken further and Singapore might experience a technical recession, or two consecutive quarters of negative growth, but this did not change its full year forecast. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar continued to be supported by fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's confirmation earlier this week that it had sold the U.S. dollar when the Sing dollar hit fresh 11-year lows of 1.8265 last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players were merely liquidating their long U.S. dollar positions, with little fresh buying of Sing dollars in sight. They added European banks were looking to buy the U.S. dollar at around 1.8020-30. \par \par \uc2  But analysts doubted the Sing dollar would extend gains in the mid term, given gloomy economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was a tad higher at 45.30 thanks to the firmer yen and the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said players liquidated their long dollar positions after the Bank of Thailand's move to tighten disclosure rules on baht trading for non-resident accounts from July 2. \par \par \uc2  Also positive for the baht, the government said it would cut corporate tax for companies listed on the Thai bourse to 25 percent from 30 percent as part of efforts to revive the sagging stock market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said oil importers were looking to buy the U.S. dollar at around 45.20-25. Baht funding costs in the offshore market were nearly flat, with the one-month forward rate at 8/13 satang per dollar against 5/15. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso eased to 50.30 as local banks covered their short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said importers were looking to sell the peso at 50.00-10, but buying orders from shipping companies were supporting the downside at 50.20-30. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines' trade surplus jumped to $1.297 billion in the first quarter from $731 million a year ago. \par \par \uc2  Political uncertainty lingered, as no clear winner had yet emerged in the race for control of the Senate. Unofficial results showed President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's People Power Coalition on course to win eight of the 13 Senate seats on offer. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged up touching a high of 1,294 on the back of a steadier yen and as Wall Street's overnight gains helped the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers in Singapore said an uncertain economic outlook and expected pre-weekend profit-taking in stocks were likely to prompt dollar buying on dips. \par \par \uc2  They said dollars bids were already emerging beyond 1,300, and were expected to cap the won around 1,290-1,295. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar inched up with the yen and on expected gains in the local stock market after Wall Street's rise. \par \par \uc2  But trade was likely to be within the 32.93-32.96 range, as players were unlikely to push the Taiwan dollar much higher on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday's widely expected rate cut would raise hopes of more foreign inflows into the stock market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the discount rate to 3.75 percent and the accommodation with collateral rate, which banks pay when using government bonds as collateral for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans, to 4.125 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was the sixth rate cut since late December, bringing the total easing to a full percentage point, with Thursday's quarter point cut twice as large as any of the previous three. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah nudged lower but was expected to stay within its recent 11,300-11,450 range despite rising political tensions, given fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Parliament is due to reconvene on May 30 when an impeachment hearing is expected to begin against President Abdurrahman Wahid for his alleged involvement in graft scandals. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said first quarter GDP data due later in the day was unlikely to impact sentiment, with the market more concerned about political developments. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the IMF praised Indonesia's move to submit revised 2001 budget assumptions to parliament, saying this would pave the way for the release of a delayed $400 million loan. The cabinet on Thursday approved the revised figures, which are likely to be presented to parliament on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The key revisions for this year include slashing the growth forecast to 3.25-3.5 percent from five percent, a rupiah exchange rate of 9,600 per dollar from 7,800, an average interest rate of 15 percent from 11.5 percent and an inflation rate of 9-9.5 percent from 7.2 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0207 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.67\tab  123.20\tab    +0.43\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8053\tab  1.8090\tab    +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    32.947\tab  32.952\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1296.00\tab 1301.90\tab    +0.46\par  Baht\tab      45.27\tab   45.33\tab    