\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late; Tracks Yen, GDP Impact Muted \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2001\par 10:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher late Friday, but off its intraday high, as it tracked the yen in a listless session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The release of expectedly weak first-quarter growth data and a bearish outlook for the economy failed to hurt the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much, as market participants were yet to recover from heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  "The market would have loved to buy U.S. dollars, but most were still licking their wounds inflicted during the acknowledged MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of (last) week," Bank of America said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  Around 0841 GMT (4:41 a.m. Friday EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.8069, down from S$1.8095 in Asia late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower, hitting an intraday low of S$1.8040, as it fell below Y123. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose slightly on the weak Singapore growth data, but most of its partial recovery came in the wake of renewed yen weakness. The dollar climbed to as high as Y123.41. \par \par \uc2  Singapore revised its estimate for economic growth in the first quarter to 4.5% from an advance estimate of 4.6% issued in April. \par \par \uc2  Significantly, the data showed that growth momentum, based on an annualized, quarter-on-quarter basis, turned negative for the first time since the Asian crisis, down by a sharp 11%, from 10% growth in the fourth quarter. \par \par \uc2  The government retained its economic growth forecast for 2001 at an already-revised 3.5%-5.5%, but added that global economic outlook is still bearish. \par \par \uc2  Ministry of Trade & Industry Chief Economist Tan Kong Yam said that while quarter-on-quarter growth momentum could contract again in the second quarter, overall year-on-year growth is expected to remain positive in the second quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  Prices of benchmark Singapore government bonds ended flat to a touch higher as market participants focused on buying off-run issues, or older bonds that are close to maturity, that have been lagging benchmark prices, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overall, trading in Singapore government bonds was very light, and the weak growth data and outlook generally supported prices. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the two-year bond was flat at 2.29%, while the yield on the five-year bond was one basis point lower at 2.96%. \par \par \uc2  On the longer end of the curve, the yield on the seven-year bond was flat at 3.34%, and the yield on the 10-year bond was one basis point lower at 3.55%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and\par are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be\par viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar interest rate swaps tracked bond yields, with the\par swap curve marginally flatter from late Thursday, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer ended one basis point lower at\par 3.52%, and the 10-year swap offer was one basis point lower at 3.74%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swap offer was at 112 basis\par points, narrower than 114 basis points Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The overnight interbank rate edged higher on pre-weekend demand for\par funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  Late Friday        Late Thursday\par                  bid      offer     bid     offer\par Overnight        2.3750%  2.5000%   1.7500%  2.0000%\par 3 Month          2.0625%  2.1875%   2.0625%  2.1875%\par 1 Year           2.1875%  2.3125%   2.1875%  2.3125%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 421 4809;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx5i0262s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
