\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Buoyed by yen, Wall St gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,075 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2001\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were buoyed in late trade on Thursday by euphoria over robust gains on Wall Street, the yen's firmer footing, and caution over moves by some regional central banks. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's consolidation was expected to be short-lived as its fundamentals remained relatively sound compared with other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I just can't imagine the yen and the euro strengthening against the dollar on a sustained basis at this juncture given fundamental pictures in Japan and the euro zone are not that bright," said a dealer at a major Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  "In emerging Asian markets, the dollar is pretty much in favour. I don't expect the Sing dollar to poke above 1.8000 or the baht above 45.00. There are lots of companies out there who will gladly pick up the dollar around those levels," he said. The market is focused on U.S. weekly jobless claims data, due at 1230 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters forecast that 395,000 people appled for unemployment benefits in the week ending May 12, up from 384,000 the previous week. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell 1.2 percent on year in April, against expectations of a 1.8 percent rise. April was the second straight month of decline, confirming market views that Singapore's economy continued to weaken. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar zipped up more than half a cent to 3-= week highs of 1.8073. \par \par \uc2  The main catalyst for the latest rise was growing fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which confirmed it had sold the U.S. dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  "Our recent comment on having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week was made to reiterate our unchanged S$ policy, notwithstanding short-term M&A flows," the MAS told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar has lost nearly four percent since the beginning of the year in part due to M&A-linked capital outflows, which are estimated to be up to $14.5 billion. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's first quarter economic survey is due out at 0000 GMT on Friday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged up to 50.05 at one stage before buying by oil companies pushed it back to 50.26. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight rates by 50 basis points following the U.S. rate cut earlier this week. This will bring the borrowing rate to 9.0 percent and the lending rate to 11.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might cut rates further next month if the U.S. Federal Reserve eased again. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht managed to stay around 45.30, after being beaten down by dollar orders from importers and companies when it tried to break above 45.15. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said the market had largely factored in news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to further tighten disclosure rules on baht trading for non-resident accounts from July 2. \par \par \uc2  "I think what the market is concerned about is not the new regulations themselves but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gesture. After all, this is just a modification of the existing rules," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  "The amount of money in the non-resident accounts is around $420 million which is not substantial," he said. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market moved left, with players unwinding dollar/baht positions in the forward market. The one-month rate was quoted at 5/15 satang per dollar and three-month at 30/45. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah enjoyed some gains as players unwound their long dollar positions due to slack corporate demand. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said a local company sold around $30 million through state banks, prompting interbank players to follow suit. \par \par \uc2  Market turnover was estimated around $150 million, which dealers said was close to the average seen in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  But they added the rupiah's outlook was still dim given the tangled economic and political problems Indonesia faces. \par \par \uc2  First quarter gross domestic product data is due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won trailed the firmer yen, with sentiment getting an additional boost from rallying local stocks. \par \par \uc2  While the yen remained the dominant influence, the won cheered over foreign funds' inflows headed for the local bourse. Foreign investors bought a net 28.3 billion won worth of local stocks for the day, though they remained net sellers of 53.9 billion won worth so far this week. \par \par \uc2  However the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unable to push through the 1,300 level, last touched on May 14. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to news the unemployment rate fell to 3.8 percent in April from 4.2 percent in March. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended at 32.952, below its opening of 32.946 due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's active U.S. dollar buying in what analysts see as a drive to keep exports competitive. \par \par \uc2  But the downside was underpinned by a steadier yen and Wall Street-inspired gains in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan stocks raked in 1.21 percent gains, dovetailing a sharp rise on Wall Street. Foreign investors bought Taiwan shares worth a net T$1.22 billion on Thursday after selling a net T$299 million in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced at an impromptu news conference that it was cutting key rates by 0.25 percentage points, its sixth easing since December. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0937 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.21\tab  123.72\tab    +0.41\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8093\tab  1.8131\tab    +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    32.952\tab  32.957\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1301.90\tab 1309.10\tab    +0.55\par  Baht\tab      45.32\tab   45.41\tab    +0.20\par  Peso\tab      50.23\tab   50.14\tab    -0.18\par  Rupiah\tab 11340.00     11410.00\tab    +0.62\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.21\tab  114.45\tab    -7.11\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8093\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.02\par  Taiwan dlr    32.952\tab  32.900\tab    -0.16\par  Korean won   1301.90\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.91\par  Baht\tab      45.32\tab   43.70\tab    -3.57\par  Peso\tab      50.23\tab   50.75\tab    +1.04\par  Rupiah\tab 11340.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -16.49\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5h03q4h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
