\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steadier as Fed decision meets hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,121 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2001\par 04:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed early Wednesday following a widely expected interest rate cut by the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said with the U.S. seen nearing the end of its easing cycle, players in the region will focus on regional problems again as the global downturn drags on. \par \par \uc2  The Fed cut the federal funds rate by 50 basis points to 4.0 percent, its lowest level in seven years. It also cut the more symbolic discount rate by the same amount to 3.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The statement announcing the cut, the fifth 50 basis point cut so far this year, said it saw excessive weakness as the main threat to the economy, and repeated concerns about falling investment spending and weak corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said slower investment spending was especially pronounced in the tech sector, to which most of Asia is exposed. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll following the cut showed most primary dealers expecting the pace of easing to slow at the Fed's next meeting on June 26-27. \par \par \uc2  The yen saw its earlier gains slip away, while the euro was little moved from overnight levels. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar firmed to 1.8150 from 1.8186 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the gain partly to comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "(The) MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within its policy band," the MAS told a local newspaper. \par \par \uc2  The MAS is believed to have sold at least $500 million when the Sing hit fresh 11-year lows of around 1.8265. \par \par \uc2  It also said the policy to allow the Sing to gradually appreciate is based on its medium-term assessment of the economy, and said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary. \par \par \uc2  "Not surprising, because everybody in the market knew it came in," a European bank dealer said. "But people are using this as an excuse to take profits." \par \par \uc2  He added better-than-expected March retail sales data also offered reasons to liquidate U.S. dollar long positions. \par \par \uc2  April non-oil domestic exports data is due on Thursday. A Reuters poll forecast a 1.8 percent on-year rise from a 2.1 percent contraction in March. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah held onto levels above 11,500, though its near-term outlook was still grim. \par \par \uc2  While the market remained long on dollar, Jakarta dealers have said local corporate demand for dollar amid the country's turbulent politics was strong. \par \par \uc2  There is also talk that around $3-$5 billiion in foreign debt will be due by mid-June, adding further pressure to the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid said on Tuesday he expected to be impeached. But he also made clear that he would not go without a fight, which would throw the country into a fresh crisis. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty about the outcome of Monday's elections, seen as a test of President Gloria Arroyo's popularity, was likely to keep the peso trapped within the 50.00-50.50 range. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said most players believed Arroyo's candidates will get most of the crucial 13 Senate seats but will fall short of a definite majority. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would consider the inflation trend in deciding whether to lower its key overnight rates following the U.S. rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate is currently at 9.5 percent and the lending rate at 11.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was marginally firmer, but was still in a familiar range as players trimmed dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  The market took heart from the Fed's latest cut, which many believed would jump-start the sagging U.S. economy - a major market for exports from Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors took news of the cabinet raising budget deficit for October 2001-September 2002 to 200 billion baht from 150 billion baht with a grain of salt. \par \par \uc2  "In theory, a bigger stimulus package should be good news," said a Bangkok dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But I guess the market was not excited because the amount is not that big. Moreover, the market wants to know how the government will channel the increased liquidity to the real economy." \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers expected the baht to loiter in the 45.40-45.50 range. Baht funding costs in the offshore market was steady at 10/15 satang for dollar for the one-month forward rate. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was steady, drifting in a thin market after opening at 1,303.0 versus the Tuesday's close of 1,303.7. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be caught between a softer yen and hopes of M&A inflows, with U.S. automobile giant General Motors expected to make an announcement next week on its talk to buy certain assets from Daewoo Motor. \par \par \uc2  Its upside is likely to be capped by recent foreign funds selling of local stocks. Foreign investors sold 95.1 billion won worth of local shares on Tuesday and around 1.5 billion won in early trade. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slipped as the yen failed to hold onto its earlier gains. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said that of the regional authorities, the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one of the most likely to follow the Fed in its easing cycle. So far this year, the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slashed rates by 75 basis points, still less than the 250 basis points that the Fed has cut. \par \par \uc2  While a rate cut typically would hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it makes local assets less attractive, the market could view further easing by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  positively as it seeks to boost economic growth. \par \par \uc2  But the market was expecting any sharp moves in the Taiwan dollar to be counteracted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0209 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.70\tab  123.27\tab    -0.35\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8143\tab  1.8182\tab    +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr     32.94\tab   32.93\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1303.00\tab 1303.20\tab    +0.02\par  Baht\tab      45.43\tab   45.50\tab    +0.15\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   50.17\tab    +0.14\par  Rupiah\tab 11365.00     11460.00\tab    +0.84\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.70\tab  114.45\tab    -7.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8143\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.29\par  Taiwan dlr     32.89\tab   32.90\tab    +0.03\par  Korean won   1303.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -2.00\par  Baht\tab      45.43\tab   43.70\tab    -3.81\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   50.75\tab    +1.30\par  Rupiah\tab 11365.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -16.67\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 D