\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Waiting for the Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,011 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2001\par 03:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 15 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on the back-foot early Tuesday as the dollar rose on hopes an anticipated Fed rate cut would help boost the economy. \par \par \uc2  But trading was likely to be subdued due to caution ahead of the Federal Open Market Committee meeting later in the day. The market is widely expecting the Fed to cut the federal funds rate by 50 basis points, which would bring it to four percent. \par \par \uc2  The yen ceded ground to the dollar amid these expectations, adding pressure to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the euro was around one-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts predicted that if the Fed cuts rates, the dollar will continue to flex its muscles, although its future strength relies on how the U.S. economy is shaping up in the second half. \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill said earlier he was not worried about a recession, nor about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values. \par \par \uc2  While the FOMC is the big economic event this week, there were also key regional and political developments in store. \par \par \uc2  Manila markets re-opened after Monday's key elections and Singapore will issue key economic data, including April non-oil exports data and the first-quarter economic survey. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won stumbled over a lower yen, although it was finding some support. \par \par \uc2  Reports that three U.S. funds were interested in buying the managerial rights and a stake in Hynix Semiconductor and a widely anticipated announcement from General Motors on its talks to take over parts of the bankrupt Daewoo Motor kept sentiment towards the won buoyed. \par \par \uc2  As with the rest of the region, the won was likely to see a quiet session ahead of the FOMC meeting. A rate cut in the U.S. was seen as beneficial to Korea as it would further hopes for a pick-up in growth in the U.S., Korea's largest export market. \par \par \uc2  However, the Bank of Korea is unlikely to follow the Fed's easing given inflationary pressures. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held off on a rate cut earlier this month due to a rise in inflation. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht edged down to 45.55 from 45.44 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said the mood was defensive on the weaker yen and Sing dollar which encouraged offshore dealers to sell the baht. They added government-linked companies and electronics exporters were moderately offering the U.S. dollar at 45.60. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Monday it was not worried about pressure on the Thai baht despite speculation the Malaysian ringgit could be allowed to devalue in future. \par \par \uc2  Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik said his ministry would review its export target for 2001 taking into account a recent slowdown in the global economy. In March, the Commerce Ministry cut its forecast for exports in 2001 to 9.46 percent from 11.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  The market kept a wary eye on the Constitutional Court's hearing of a graft case against Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was basically steady edged up and was likely to gain some more ground as Monday's poll went through without a major hickup and raised hopes President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's supporters will win enough seats to ensure smooth governance through her term. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market perception was that Arroyo's supporters will win eight of the 13 Senate seats and a decent majority in the 262 House of Representatives. \par \par \uc2  However, final election results will not be available for several days and that would infuse some uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  Allegations of fraud and rigging traditionally follow polls in the Philippines and litigation into such matters usually drag on for months. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the trading range for the day should be within 50.00-50.50, but players will be on the watch for any bad news to quickly go dollar long. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar hovered around the 1.8200 mark as overnight losses of the yen and euro encouraged players go U.S. dollar long. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to keep players cautious when treading beyond the 1.8200 mark and they will also be on the watch for any trading cues from the March retail sales data due Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the U.S. dollar was expected to be strong at around 1.8170-1.8180 range, where local banks were selling U.S. dollars on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Most U.S. dollar offers are now expected to have lined up at 1.8225-1.8230. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was trapped in a narrow range, caught between equity-linked foreign inflows and importer dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened unchanged at 32.882 before dipping to 32.890. Demand from foreign funds later lifted it to 32.887 at 0122 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been net buyers of local stocks since April 30, buying a total T$34.982 billion worth of shares as of Monday. \par \par \uc2  The yen's retreat and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should cap the Taiwan dollar's upside at 32.82, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0138 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.26\tab  122.72\tab    -0.44\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8180\tab  1.8145\tab    -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr     32.89\tab   32.88\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1302.20\tab 1297.40\tab    -0.37\par  Baht\tab      45.52\tab   45.43\tab    -0.20\par  Peso\tab      50.29\tab   50.25\tab    -0.08\par  Rupiah\tab 11460.00     11400.00\tab    -0.52\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.26\tab  114.45\tab    -7.15\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8180\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.48\par  Taiwan dlr     32.83\tab   32.90\tab    +0.21\par  Korean won   1302.20\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.94\par  Baht\tab      45.52\tab   43.70\tab    -4.00\par  Peso\tab      50.29\tab   50.75\tab    +0.91\par  Rupiah\tab 11460.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -17.36\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx5f003xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
