\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Directionless, Fed, US data eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,138 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2001\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed bag late Friday as the market was driven by domestic leads while players kept a low profile ahead of April retail sales data at 1230 GMT and Tuesday's Federal Reserve rate-setting meeting. \par \par \uc2  The market has largely factored in another 50 basis point rate cut, but debate will continue over how much more the Fed will need to cut to stimulate U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. is a major market for exports from Asia and any move that to keep its economy growing is positive to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast U.S. April retail sales rose 0.2 percent overall after a decline of 0.2 percent in March. \par \par \uc2  In the region, the Philippine peso hovered in a snug range, with activity muted ahead of congressional elections on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar recouped some lost ground on talk of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but gains were stunted by persistent demand for the U.S. dollar to fund overseas asset purchases by local companies. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso traded in a narrow 50.45-50.55 range for most of the day helped by easing fears of violence ahead of Monday's Senate polls and on an overall lack of dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  Total turnover was a mere $117.5 million, compared with Thursday's $137 million. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Manila said the peso's upside was capped by interbank players and importers seeking dollars on dips. \par \par \uc2  With most players already long of dollars, a growing perception the polls would pass peacefully resulted in some unwinding of those positions. \par \par \uc2  Philippine financial markets will be closed on Monday for the election. Trade will resume on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar edged down in thin trading to 1.8140 from early highs of 1.8120. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said European banks and U.S. funds took profits on long U.S. dollar positions, but importers and corporates were looking to sell the Sing dollar at 1.8120. \par \par \uc2  They said the market was wary of further MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given speculation they had sold at least $500 million in the last two sessions. The MAS said on Thursday it does not comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Speculation is rife whether or not the MAS is going to shift its tightening monetary stance to neutral to weather a slowdown. The Sing dollar has fallen in recent sessions to levels analysts believe to be beyond the MAS' tightening policy band. \par \par \uc2  "I think the MAS was tactical if they did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it has to introduce some sort of uncertainty in the market," a U.S. bank analyst said. \par \par \uc2  "If people are sure that its monetary stance is neutral, which in reality it is, no one would hold the Sing dollar because the interest rates are lower than the U.S. yet the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is depreciating. It makes no economic sense." INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah eased but kept off its session low of 11,260 after state banks were spotted selling dollars near 11,200, the 38 percent retracement of the dollar's steep April 26-May 1 slide. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said initial dollar buying was sparked by news of a late Thursday bomb blast in a dormitory in the suburbs in which two people died. \par \par \uc2  However, fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and relatively subdued dollar demand from corporates tempered the rupiah selling spree. \par \par \uc2  The market largely ignored comments by the IMF's spokesman who said the government's proposed fiscal package which targets a budget deficit of 3.7 percent could form a good basis for restarting talks on stalled lending. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market had keenly tracked the twists and turns in Jakarta's relations with the IMF and would react only after a decision is taken on disbursement of a $400 million loan tranche suspended since December. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said the bank was not certain if domestic interest rates already around 21-month highs would be cut or raised. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was locked in a tight 45.40-45.53 range, wedged between exporter dollar offers and a lack of demand for the baht. \par \par \uc2  Some Bangkok dealers said dollar/baht looked set to break out of its recent consolidative phase and head higher. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Friday showed the external account remained weak. Although Thailand managed to eke out a trade surplus of $38 million in the first quarter, a finance ministry official said its trade balance in April would be in deficit. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won hovered around the 1,300 mark supported by export and equity related inflows. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Hong Kong said interbank players worries over the yen, which retreated from its recent highs against the dollar, kept the won's upside capped. \par \par \uc2  Interest was subdued ahead of the U.S. retail sales data and the Fed's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  They said talk General Motors was planning to make an announcement on its talks to buy part of the bankrupt Daewoo Motor also kept players cautious. \par \par \uc2  Local newspapers quoted Korean officials saying the deal was in the final stages. Dealers said a successful sale of Daewoo was likely to help the won in terms of both flows and sentiment. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged up to 32.87 from 32.91 earlier thanks to buying by U.S. banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said firmer stocks also lifted sentiment, with the benchmark TAIEX ending up more than two percent on buying by state-linked funds. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Taiwan dollar might get a boost if Taiwan's weighting in Morgan Stanley Capital International (MSCI)'s global indices was increased on May 19. \par \par \uc2  A local newspaper reported the planned adjustment to Taiwan's weighting would bring in an additional US$1.3 billion annually over the next five years. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0853 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.31\tab  122.20\tab    -0.09\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8128\tab  1.8188\tab    +0.33\par  Taiwan dlr    32.882\tab  32.884\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1300.70\tab 1305.00\tab    +0.33\par  Baht\tab      45.44\tab   45.41\tab    -0.07\par  Peso\tab      50.25\tab   50.59\tab    +0.68\par  Rupiah\tab 11250.00     11150.00\tab    -0.89\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.31\tab  114.45\tab    -6.43\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8128\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.21\par  Taiwan dlr    32.882\tab  32.900\tab    +0.05\par  Korean won   1300.70\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.82\par  Baht\tab      45.44\tab   43.70\tab    -3.83\par  Peso\tab      50.25\tab   5