\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS seen curbing Sing dlr drop - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2001\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 10 (Reuters) - Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) in recent days is cementing fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have lost patience with recent exchange rate weakness, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar reached highs of around 1.8170 to the U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling dollars around 1.8220/30. It was quoted at 1.8187/97 by 0815 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The MAS had no comment. "We do not normally comment on our market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said an MAS official. \par \par \uc2  Given estimates of aggressive overseas expansion by Singapore firms, worsening external economic conditions and rising political risks in the neighbourhood, drawing a rigid line in the sand may prove a bit difficult. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts believe an aggressive rejoinder to the Sing dollar's drop to 11-year lows around 1.8270 early this week was aimed at putting to rest speculation the MAS was shifting its monetary stance from a policy favouring a gradual appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was behind rather heavy U.S. dollar sales, led by local banks, late Wednesday that pushed the Sing dollar up to 1.8190 and was also active on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Several smoothening \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly in London and New York trading time had been spotted since the Sing dollar breached the 1.82 level against the U.S. dollar in early April, they said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a major local bank said because of genuine dollar demand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept a low profile despite the Sing dollar drifting far from 1.8000-1.8050 - what he believed to be the weaker end of the MAS policy band. \par \par \uc2  "But they would certainly discourage the market from taking this as a shift in its stance," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said rising interbank offer rates in the money market also indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was draining liquidity, in another effort to bolster the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  The on-and-off speculation on the MAS's stance of a "gently appreciating band" picked up after the MAS said last week inflation was not a near-term threat from the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar is being impacted by both flows and sentiment...so drawing too many rigid lines in the sand may not be appropriate," said David Simmonds, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  "But there must be a limit to it (decline) or otherwise it does require a close scrutiny of the monetary policy," he added. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx5a00gd1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
