\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Caught in yen's downdraft, Fed watched. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,094 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2001\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved lower early Thursday after the yen slipped to one-week lows against the dollar on stock losses and waning optimism about Japan's new government. \par \par \uc2  Fresh economic data from Japan indicated that an economic recovery might still be elusive. Lending by Japanese banks fell 3.4 percent on year in April, the 40th consecutive month of decline. The wholesale price index also fell 0.1 percent on year in April. \par \par \uc2  Market players were likely to keep a low profile ahead of the May 15 Federal Open Market Committee meeting. Most analysts expected the Fed to cut key rates by another 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Local factors were also weighing on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Uncertainty in the run-up to the Philippines' Senate elections on Monday kept the dollar well-bid agains the peso. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar continued to be dampened by talk of merger and acquisitions, though rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday should cap its downside. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Asian Development Bank warned that Asia would face slower growth over the next two years, but said fears of a new regional crisis were overstated. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar eased past 1.8200 after hitting a high of 1.8190 late Wednesday for the second session in a row, on talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said heavy selling of dollar by local banks around 1.8250-60, with U.S. funds joining in later, sparked speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Local corporates and some foreign banks were still chasing the dollar around 1.8220, and dealers said dollar demand was stronger near 1.8200. \par \par \uc2  But they added wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cap the Sing's downside, keeping it within the 1.8210-1.8260 range. \par \par \uc2  However, players who believe local companies need to buy more dollars to hedge their recent investments abroad would attempt to breach 1.8267 touched Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won shadowed the yen's movements, but exporters' dollar sales and foreign investors' equity-linked inflows were expected to cap its downside. \par \par \uc2  However, the won has been unable to break resistance of around 1,293, a level last seen on March 21 when it fell past 1,300. Dealers said there was genuine dollar demand from local importers waiting to buy dollar on dips towards 1,295. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said in the absence of any big moves in the dollar/yen, the won was relegated to stay within narrow ranges. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, charts showed volatility in the won has fallen by over 40 percent since May 2 as the price action has narrowed increasingly in recent session. However, analysts also noted the won has been stronger than its 14-day moving average. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht ticked down from 45.59 late Wednesday, tracking the softer yen. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said trading was lacklustre as offshore dealers were on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  They added the baht was supported around 45.65 by buying interest from food and garment exporters, while foreign banks were keen to sell around 45.48-50. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's comments that Thailand's economy is expected to grow 3.5-5.0 percent in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand has forecast GDP growth of 3-4.5 percent in 2001, against 4.3 percent in 2000. But the bank said in late April the economy would expand by 2.5-4.0 percent this year. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's Constitutional Court will reach a verdict by August on whether Thaksin is guilty of deliberately concealing some of his wealth. If found guilty, Thaksin will be banned from political office for five years. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah continued to loiter around the 11,000 mark, enjoying the relative calm in Indoneisa's usually stormy political scene. \par \par \uc2  However, the lack of dollar inflows and sinking sentiment over the country's economic and political woes prevented the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from making any substantial gains. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Bank Indonesia said late Wednesday economic growth in the second quarter was expected to come in at 3.8 percent, slower than the first quarter. Indonesia's economy has been badly hobbled by the weak rupiah as shaky politics have blocked economic reforms, stalled the IMF's $5 billion latest lending programme, and discouraged foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was pressured by worries ahead of the May 14 Senate polls, and dealers expected it to hit lower levels given the lack of dollar supply. \par \par \uc2  They said some exporters' dollar offers were expected around 50.80, but sentiment was bullish on dollar given the uncertainty over the outcome of the polls, which are seen as a test of President Gloria Arroyo's popularity. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Wednesday gross international reserves as of end-April slipped to $14.5 billion from $14.7 billion the previous month due to payments by the government of maturing external debt. \par \par \uc2  The bank's monetary board will hold its weekly meeting later in the day, but most analysts expected it to keep rates steady ahead of the Fed's May 15 meeting. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar nestled in its recent range, with trading expected to remain listless. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Taipei noted late Wednesday some outflows from foreign funds, which could pressure the local dollar lower if they pick up steam. \par \par \uc2  However, players have continued unwinding their long dollar positions around 32.90, a level that the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is defending. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed volatility in the Taiwan dollar has remained below one since April 19. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0215 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.15\tab  121.57\tab    -0.47\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8230\tab  1.8210\tab    -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr     32.89\tab   32.88\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1301.70\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      45.53\tab   45.49\tab    -0.09\par  Peso\tab      50.68\tab   50.64\tab    -0.08\par  Rupiah\tab 11185.00     11070.00\tab    -1.03\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.15\tab  114.45\tab    -6.30\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8230\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.74\par  Taiwan dlr     32.83\tab   32.90\tab    +0.21\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.90\par  Baht\tab      45.53\tab   43.70\tab    -4.02\par  Peso\tab      50.68\tab   50.75\tab    +0.14\par  Rupiah\tab 11185.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -15.33\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  