\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Mixed, poor U.S. data weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2001\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 9 (Reuters) - Most Asian equities were mixed \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday in cautious trading after lower U.S. productivity \par \par \uc2  data and a jump in labour costs raised concerns about inflation \par \par \uc2  and a slowing economy. \par \par \uc2      Productivity in the first quarter in the United States fell \par \par \uc2  for the first time in six years, but unit labour costs posted a \par \par \uc2  bigger-than-expected gain, the largest since the last quarter \par \par \uc2  of 1997. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Tokyo, the benchmark Nikkei average\tab    fell for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second straight session as investors sought more details on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's much-hyped reforms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's time now to see a follow-through (on reforms)," an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity analyst in Tokyo said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Lower House was due to hold a question-and-answer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session later in the day on Koizumi's debut policy speech made\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday. The opposition camp was expected to attack him for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being short on concrete details.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "He's got to show results within 100 days. But we know\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nothing happens overnight in Japan, except for earthquakes,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the analyst said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan is due to hold an election for the Upper House by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late July. Speculation is rife the ruling Liberal Democratic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Party might call for an early election for the more powerful\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lower House to use Koizumi's sky-high popularity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nikkei's dip weighed on the yen , which slipped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 121.84 at one point but worries about an evident U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic slowdown underpinned it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par M&A VS MAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar kept a softer tone at around 1.8240\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the U.S. dollar, suffering from prospects of further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par merger and acquisition-related capital outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The latest discomfort came from media reports that United\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overseas Bank had offered to buy Hong Kong's HKCB\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank for US$692 million. HKCB denied the talk but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said it was enough to sour the Sing dollar's prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the weakening Sing dollar and a lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suggested it would shift its monetary policy to neutral from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tightening at its mid-year review in July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some said the current monetary stance already suggested\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a neutral policy setting given the Sing dollar's exchange rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which includes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen and euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Singapore doesn't need to be tightening monetary policy at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this stage and in my view will not do so," David Simmonds,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Salomon Smith Barney, told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said on a trade-weighted basis, the Singapore dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushing through what he perceived as the MAS' "neutral"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par parameters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Simmonds said he expected the MAS to reiterate over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next week or two that it was not returning to a loose monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "During this period of intense M&A related-noise in any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par case it's wise not to be drawing too many rigid lines in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sand."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINES EYES RATE CUT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the Philippines, hopes for a rate cut boosted the debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, especially on the short end .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds its weekly monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy meeting on Thursday. The bank has said it was more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par biased to cut rates to buoy the economy, rather than cutting to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defend the fragile peso .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The key overnight borrowing rate is now at 9.5 percent and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lending rate at 11.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said lower rates would help the Philippines to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par service its mountain of foreign debt totalling $52.06 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the end of 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But they added the market kept a wary eye on Senate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elections next Monday, which weighed on overall sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0901 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.57\tab  121.89\tab    +0.26\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8210\tab  1.8240\tab    +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    32.879\tab  32.875\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1302.00\tab    +0.02\par  Baht\tab      45.49\tab   45.57\tab    +0.18\par  Peso\tab      50.64\tab   50.46\tab    -0.36\par  Rupiah\tab 11070.00     10930.00\tab    -1.26\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.57\tab  114.45\tab    -5.86\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8210\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.64\par  Taiwan dlr    32.879\tab  32.900\tab    +0.06\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.90\par  Baht\tab      45.49\tab   43.70\tab    -3.93\par  Peso\tab      50.64\tab   50.75\tab    +0.22\par  Rupiah\tab 11070.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -14.45\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0901 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  14084.85     14289.05\tab    -1.43\par  Hong Kong   13585.14     13540.81\tab    +0.33\par  Singapore    1687.22\tab 1701.98\tab    -0.87\par  Taipei\tab  5232.64\tab 5176.71\tab    +1.08\par  Seoul\t