\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady on yen, lack of domestic cues. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2001\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 9 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held within their recent ranges late on Wednesday, helped by a lack of fresh domestic leads and a steady yen. \par \par \uc2  Even the more volatile rupiah and peso traded within a narrow band as markets waited for a May 11 meeting of top Indonesian politicians and the May 14 Senate polls in the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen's retracement from around 124 levels in late April was supporting most regionals on the downside but their upside was capped by persistent signs of weakening growth in the U.S. - Asia's largest export market. \par \par \uc2  The latest data indicating a further slowing included a drop in productivity and a rise in labour costs. \par \par \uc2  For more clues on the U.S. economy, markets will focus on Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greespan's speech at a banking conference on Thursday and on Friday's April retail sales report. \par \par \uc2  The events will set the tone ahead of the Fed's May 15 policy meeting where it is widely expected to cut another 50 basis points off its 4.5 percent funds rate. \par \par \uc2  The yen was under pressure in early European trade, helped by a fall on the Nikkei and as the euphoria over new Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi faded. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded in a tight range near its three-week lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was sandwiched between fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk of M&A outflows, which prevented a significant rebound from its 11-year lows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said most of the day's trade was within a 1.830-1.860 range with U.S. names and local banks buying dollars on dips. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said last week's comments by the MAS and poor economic data had encouraged players to probe weaker levels. \par \par \uc2  They said the risk of the Malaysian ringgit being repegged lower was another factor weighing on the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit is believed to form a sizeable component in the trade-weighted basket the MAS uses to manage the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht edged higher against the dollar, thanks to exporter dollar sales and foreign inflows to Thai assets, dealers in Singapore and Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drifted in a snug 45.52-45.62 range, in the absence of strong domestic leads. But it was expected to be top-heavy in the near term due to poor fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  A finance ministry official said on Wednesday Thailand switched to a monthly trade deficit in April after surpluses in the previous two months. \par \par \uc2  Based on about 85 percent of trade information for April, the deficit stood at US$56 million. Consumer confidence also fell in April from the previous month, according to a university survey. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, dealers said there was good demand for dollar/baht outrights in three-and six-month tenors. The three-month rate was quoted at 45/60 satang per dollar, and the six-month rate at 80/110. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  Falling local shares and worries over the U.S. economy nudged the won slightly lower as it spent most of the session glumly following the yen. \par \par \uc2  With dollar/yen stalling, the won has been mired in a narrow range of 1,295-1,305 since the beginning of the week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said unless the yen made any significant moves, the won was likely to continue trading in a narrow range, trapped between local importers' dollar bids and foreign investors' equity-related inflows. \par \par \uc2  On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won was at 1,302/3 against 1,301.8/2.8 late Tuesday and the three-month was at 1,306/7 from 1,306/7. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah loitered just under the 11,000 level, plagued by the usual suspects of a lack of dollar inflows and Jakarta's volatile politics. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said while local corporate dollar demand still lurked, players were unwilling to take fresh long dollar positions as a resolution to the current political crisis may be reached soon. \par \par \uc2  Major political parties are due to meet on Friday, fueling talk a compromise may be reached to determine the future of President Abdurrahman Wahid, who could possibly face impeachment. Bank Indonesia warned late Wednesday that economic growth was likely to be slower in the second quarter while inflation was set to rise. The country's economic problems have been compounded by the weak rupiah and persistent political instability. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso closed lower at 50.65 against the open of 55.44 as gains inspired by overseas workers' remittances were countered by dollar bargain hunting as the market remained nervous ahead of the congressional election on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The market was factoring in potential rate cuts after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said last week that it was biased towards cutting key interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its benchmark interest rates by 550 basis points since mid-December, more than reversing a 400 basis point hike in October which was aimed at shoring up the peso. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said those aggressive cuts might not be enough to boost the economy, and it was important for the government to quickly shift from rhetoric into action. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly, low domestic interest rates alone may not be enough to spur growth. However, the ball is no longer in the hands of monetary authorities," Jojo Gonzales, head of strategy and economics at Merrill Lynch, said in a report. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar closed a touch lower on Wednesday after gaining on the back of foreign fund inflows in the past seven sessions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar buying in NDF markets weighed on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but profit taking at 32.90, the top end of its recent range, helped limit the downside. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg said poor export data released on Tuesday kept offshore interest in dollar/Taiwan dollar forwards and it expected the spot rate to trade above 32.90 in the next few days. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0903 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.58\tab  121.89\tab    +0.25\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8218\tab  1.8240\tab    +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    32.879\tab  32.875\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1302.00\tab    +0.02\par  Baht\tab      45.49\tab   45.57\tab    +0.18\par  Peso\tab      50.64\tab   50.46\tab    -0.36\par  Rupiah\tab 11075.00     10930.00\tab    -1.31\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.58\tab  114.45\tab    -5.86\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8218\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.68\par  Taiwan dlr    32.879\tab  32.900\tab    +0.06\par  Korean won   1301.70\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.90\par  Baht