\par\par \b \uc2  Politics plagues peso again, Sing dlr subdued. \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2001\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0215 GMT - The Philippine peso was well submerged under the 51 per dollar level as the market fretted over a huge rally by supporters of former president Joseph Estrada. \par \par \uc2  - Estrada arrested on Wednesday on economic plunder charges - punishable by death - and thousands now gathered near where he is being held. \par \par \uc2  - Manila dealers say local corporates, including state-run and oil companies, hedging dollar exposure and exporters holding onto their dollars. \par \par \uc2  - Market also anxious about lower regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Argentina, as Philippines is viewed as most vulnerable in Asia to further deterioration in Argentina's economic problems. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers say 51.50 viewed as next dollar resistance, last seen on January 19 when peso strengthened some 14 percent ahead of Estrada's resignation. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said he did not expect capital flight or speculative activity from recent political developments. Adds will not raise rates to help peso. \par \par \uc2  - Singapore dollar bouncing around 1.8200 with local banks' dollar short-covering matched by offers from U.S. names. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers say Sing dollar tracking yen, but market still wary of pushing dollar/Sing higher after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  around Thursday's high of 1.8245. \par \par \uc2  - Market also watching weekend developments in Jakarta, where supporters of President Wahid will hold vigil on Sunday ahead of key parliamentary session. \par \par \uc2  - Indonesian rupiah languishes with foreign and local banks bidding dollar/rupiah to high so far of 12,180. \par \par \uc2  - Local corporate dollar demand expected at 12,100 amid ongoing political upheaval. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta dealers say Bank Indonesia and state banks not in market yet to defend rupiah. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4r01872\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
