\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Lifted by firmer yen before holiday. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2001\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 12 (Reuters) - The firmer yen bumped Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencier\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher in light trade late Thursday ahead of the Easter break. \par \par \uc2  This report will not appear on Friday, April 13, due to the Easter holiday in most of Asia and the Songkran holiday in Thailand. Please see and for reports on the Korean won and Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  The yen extended its recent gains, taking advantage of speculation over U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill's commitment to the strong dollar policy. Those gains lent particular support to the North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was earlier upset by media reports the U.S. National Association for Manufacturers will meet with O'Neill later this month to complain about the strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, the euro edged slightly higher. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the outlook for the yen and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still cloudy at best, given slowing external demand and the limping tech sector. \par \par \uc2  On the domestic front, Korea's finance ministry said earlier it would expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and use dollar/won forwards to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  And the Bank of Thailand said it was content with the current level of the baht. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won extended its gains alongside the yen, with wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helping. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said stop-loss dollar sales were triggered around 1,330 and 1,322. "The market was quite long on dollar anyway. So the yen and the concerns over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are good reasons to bail out of these positions," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Korean authorities continued to harden their line towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The Finance Ministry said it would push local banks to repay borrowings owed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to boost reserves. \par \par \uc2  It did not elaborate how it intended to use dollar/won forwards to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, nor whether that included the offshore non-deliverable forward market. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the market largely ignored the rhetoric, given the lack of detail. A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst also said the onshore forward market was relatively small. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Finance Minister Jin Nyum said the government would not step into the market to support the won unless it saw panic or speculation, adding however that it would coordinate any action with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht traded in a tight range with low volumes for most of the day as players avoided taking aggressive positions ahead of a long weekend. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets in Bangkok will be closed from April 13-16 to celebrate the Songkran festival that marks the Thai New Year. They will reopen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said a firmer yen and fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept most players from taking long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said poor fundamentals and continuing equity outflows suggested the baht will weaken in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand's assistant governor Chetthavee Charoenpitaks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was satisfied with the current level and stability of the baht, which he attributed to stability in the yen. \par \par \uc2  He declined to respond when asked whether a recent strengthening of the baht was due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR The Sing dollar extended gains to above 1.8030 with trading volume picking up in the afternoon after U.S. names sold dollar/Sing as the yen probed two-week highs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investment banks and local banks were keen to buy the dollar at 1.8025-30, with others squaring their positions ahead of the long weekend. \par \par \uc2  The market will now focus on the release of non-oil domestic exports on Tuesday, with a poor figure expected to hound the Sing dollar to decade troughs of 1.8235 hit on April 2. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said despite no improvement in the grim economic outlook, fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would support the downside at 1.8180 for now. \par \par \uc2  In February, non-oil domestic exports rose a worse-than-expected 5.4 percent on year from nine percent in January. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was a shade higher from late Wednesday levels after touching a low of 50.15 in light and sporadic offshore trade. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Manila were closed for the Easter break and will reopen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said only a few banks were squaring their positions before the Easter holidays and given low volumes, the moves were exaggerated. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rode the yen's coat-tails, poking above 32.90 as players trimmed long dollar positions after the yen probed two-week highs against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had not heard of any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Taiwan market on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Recent gains in the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index , which is taken as a strong barometer for the island's exports, also boosted sentiment, they said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign fund buying of local stocks also underpinned the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Wednesday, they bought shares worth a net T$1.961 billion, ending an eight-session net selling streak of T$21.751. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah came off an intraday high of 10,380 due to dollar demand from a multi-national company and state banks in a thin pre-holiday market. \par \par \uc2  But its downside was underpinned by hopes the IMF team's visit to Jakarta would lead to the disbursement of a $400 million loan delayed since last year. \par \par \uc2  "We do not think this visit will result in an LOI (letter of intent), but are encouraged that the likelihood of one is increasing," said an IDEAglobal report. \par \par \uc2  "However, the overall picture still remains tenous...IMF is also concerned about budget deficit and says market may not have priced in possibility of deficit running out of control," it said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's steadier tone has eased pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to directly or indirectly prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia on Thursday kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in the rupiah interbank money market unchanged. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are among the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tools to manage liquidity. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0814 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.37\tab  124.06\tab    +0.56\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8038\tab  1.8052\tab    +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    32.909\tab  32.920\tab    +0.03\par  Korean won   1316.30\tab 1320.00\tab    +0.28\par  Baht\tab      45.36\tab   45.38\tab    +0.04\par  Peso\tab      49.35\tab   49.40\tab    +0.10\par  Rupiah\tab 10560.00     10619.00\tab    +0.56\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7999\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.37\tab  114.45\tab    -7.23\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8038\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.73\par  Taiwan dlr    32.909\tab  32.900\tab    -0.03\par  Korean won   1316.30\tab 1277.00\tab    -2.99\par  Baht\tab      45.36\tab   43.70\tab    -3.66\par  Peso\tab      49.35\tab   50.75\tab    +2.84\par  Rupiah\tab 10560.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -10.32\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7999\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4c026yy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
