\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Climb with yen's help,c.bank worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2001\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eked out gains early Wednesday, buoyed by the steady yen and persistent worries over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen held onto recent mild gains, thanks to the lingering effects of Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa's cautionary remarks on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But the euro was the biggest loser, with concerns the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hold rates dragging it down. Dealers said losses in euro/yen were weighing on the dollar/yen as well. \par \par \uc2  Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted selling dollars in the market on Tuesday, keeping up recent direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In contrast, Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains on Tuesday while Thai and Singapore authorities were largely absent. \par \par \uc2  But with players still on the look-out for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market was happy to carry on unwinding dollar longs. Wall Street's overnight gains were also lifting the mood on local bourses, with the improved spirits spilling into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts pointed out Tuesday's downgrade of Singapore's 2001 growth forecast and Taiwan's 2001 export growth forecast indicated tough times ahead for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Asia feels the impact of the U.S. slowdown. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar bounced more than a cent to 1.8060 from Tuesday lows of 1.8200, after fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged profit-taking on long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said on Tuesday it was keeping its policy bias towards a gradual appreciation of the local dollar and was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it within its policy band. \par \par \uc2  Players, who had speculated the MAS might have shifted its bias to neutral, were unwinding dollar longs, but were looking to buy on dips to 1.8020-30, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is significant change in sentiment. It's a good chance to buy cheap dollars," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But the Sing might reverse course if Hong Kong's Dao Heng Bank confirms talk Singapore's DBS Group is set to make a bid for it in a deal valued up to $5.78 billion. \par \par \uc2  A spokeswoman for Dao Heng said it will likely make an announcement later in the day. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht chalked up modest gains to 45.37 from Tuesday's low of 45.71, thanks to offshore banks unwinding long dollar positions as the yen and the Sing firmed. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they were seeking to buy dollar on dips to around 45.30 given weak economic fundamentals and potential political risks. \par \par \uc2  Lawyers for Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra denied on Tuesday accusations he hide assets and argued his wife was responsible for handling his business affairs. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's Constitutional Court heard its third day of evidence on Tuesday to decide whether to uphold a ruling Thaksin filed false asset returns when he was a minister in the 1990s. \par \par \uc2  If the court confirms the ruling, Thaksin faces a five-year ban from politics. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs offshore were vitrually flat, with the one-month rate at 17/25 satang per dollar from 17/45 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged higher on the back of gains in U.S. equities and a firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  The KOSPI rose over 2 percent at the open, helped by the Nasdaq's 6 percent rise and a 9.45 percent gain in the Philadelphia Stock Exchange's semiconductor sub-index \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said given recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities, players were avoiding long dollar positions for now. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said with doubts still hanging over the yen's outlook and prospects of a turnaround in electronics sector demand, the dollar was likely to maintain its safe haven status. \par \par \uc2  "With global economic prospects deteriorating and importers remaining unhedged any dips in the dollar are likely to be only temporary," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg, maintaining a dollar/won near-term target of 1,400. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar nudged up further, taking heart from the firmer yen and won as well as gains on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Singapore said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to cap any sharp rise in the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's trade data suggested Taiwan's economy was slowing in line with the U.S. and because of weak domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday exports in March fell 1.8 percent on-year, while imports were down 13.1 percent, leading to a slash of 2001 export growth forecast to just 0.5 percent, against an earlier forecast of 4.21 percent. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah clamoured higher with local corporate dollar demand falling quiet as an IMF team began its review of Jakarta's progress in economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was likely to be thin with players riveted on the 12-14 day review conducted by the IMF team. \par \par \uc2  The Fund said late Tuesday in Washington the long-awaited mission would have to assess some outstanding issues before a delayed $400 million loan could be approved. \par \par \uc2  Approval of the loan and a new letter of intent with the IMF are key to triggering a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling with the Paris Club of official creditors. \par \par \uc2  Among the issues that have yet to be resolved between the Fund and Jakarta is the controversial plan to change \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. Indonesian leaders have been elusive as to whether they will stick to the plan, which the IMF fears may compromise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's short-lived independence. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was gained some ground on the back of firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar remittances from overseas workers ahead of the Easter break. \par \par \uc2  Manila's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will close at noon on Wednesday and will re-open on Monday. \par \par \uc2  An IMF official said late Tuesday the Philippines would likely see its economy grow by around three percent this year. \par \par \uc2  Markus Rodlauer, who is leading an IMF mission currently in Manila, added that the Fund generally agreed with the government's economic targets, stressing the particular importance of meeting the deficit target. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0154 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.09\tab  124.40\tab    +0.25\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8035\tab  1.