\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Clouded by easier yen, bleak outlook. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2001\par 03:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stuck within recent weak ranges early Tuesday as the dollar made gains against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2  Fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to keep players on their toes, though a weaker yen and increasing evidence of slowing growth would leave demand for the dollar intact on dips, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  A steadier yen combined with verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Asian central banks in the past few sessions has kept most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  off their recent lows. \par \par \uc2  However, some of the regionals have sustained more damage on conflicting comments by officials and politicians. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said with key U.S. economic data including retail sales and the producer price index for March expected later in the week, markets might adopt a cautious approach. \par \par \uc2  In early Asian trade, the yen was struggling the wrong side of 125 as fresh economic data confirmed the market's negative view on the prospects for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said on Monday the March domestic wholesale price index dropped 0.5 percent from last year, the steepest fall in two years. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also under pressure ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy-setting meeting on Wednesday. Most analysts expect at least a 25-basis point cut in the bank's 4.75 percent benchmark rate. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was steady in early trade on wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected authorities to keep it within a 1,340-1,345 range. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea sold an estimated $200 million on Monday after a sale of upto $500 million on Friday following weeks of verbal threats on the won's declines in line with the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more worried on the yen/won cross rate and some believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were intended to keep the cross rate at around 10.60. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more aggressive after the cross rate went as high as 11 last Thursday," a dealer at a European bank in Hong Kong said. Yen/won was last quoted at 10.69/74. \par \par \uc2  Korea competes with Japan in a number of export markets. \par \par \uc2  The won's declines against the dollar, however, have inflated import prices that rose 0.8 percent in March from the previous month. Export prices rose 1.8 percent in March. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was clinging to 10,800 as the market waited for an IMF team to begin reviewing Jakarta's economic reforms on Wednesday, a crucial step towards a new letter of intent, which would secure the release of a delayed $400 million loan. \par \par \uc2  The letter would also trigger a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling deal with the Paris Club of official creditors. \par \par \uc2  But analysts have cautioned against high expectations as the IMF and Jakarta may still have differences over controversial proposals to change \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. \par \par \uc2  A senior economics official said on Monday the goverment agreed in principle with an independent panel's review of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reforms. He did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Attorney General Marzuki Darusman said the government would stand by its insistence that the entire \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board resign when the changes took effect. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was expected to come under pressure with local importers seeking dollars ahead of the Easter break. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Manila were closed on Monday for the Valour Day holiday and will be closed again on Thursday and Friday for Easter. \par \par \uc2  Given the dearth of fresh domestic factors, the peso has been tracking other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have been hobbled by the U.S. slowdown and softer yen. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar crept down to touch the 1.82 mark in early trading, putting it perilously close to decade lows of 1.8235 hit last week. \par \par \uc2  The latest upset was caused by a worse-than-expected growth figure for the first quarter and a bigger-than-expected cut in Singapore's 2001 growth forecast. \par \par \uc2  The government said the economy grew just 4.6 percent year-on-year in the first quarter of 2001, due to a significant slowdown in the manufacturing sector. A Reuters poll of 10 economists had predicted 5.9 percent growth. \par \par \uc2  It also cut the growth forecast for 2001 to 3.5 to 5.5 percent from five to seven percent. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the market was caught short of U.S. dollars and players were scrambling to cover their positions. \par \par \uc2  But they saw no sizeable orders related to news Singapore's DBS Group was set to make a bid for Dao Heng Bank in a deal valued at up to $5.78 billion. Analysts emphasised that bears were merely using the news as an excuse to further bid up dollar/Sing. \par \par \uc2  "While DBS are likely to have already covered their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, the news added to the constant flow of Singaporean corporates looking to acquire overseas investment," said UBS Warburg \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mansoor Mohi-uddin said in a report. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT The baht was riveted to a tight 45.65-45.75 range in early morning trading after rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hefty profit-taking on U.S. dollar longs pushed it off 37-month lows of 45.85 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But Bangkok dealers said local banks were keen to buy the U.S. dollar on dips at 45.50-55. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market were a tad firmer, with the one-month forward rate at 37/47 satang per dollar from 30/60 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was edging closer to the support level of 33.00, which dealers expected it to breach due to the weaker yen and expectations of poor trade data, to be released at 0245 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expected March trade data to show negative year-on-year export growth. The island recorded a trade surplus of $1.059 billion in February. \par \par \uc2  A comment by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Perng Fai-nan that the exchange rate needed to be flexible and reflect changes in the global financial environment was likely to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the defensive, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said players were still looking to buy the U.S. dollar on dips to 32.90, with stops placed at 32.85. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0138 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.83\tab  125.21\tab    +0.30\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8155\tab  1.8155\tab    +0.00\par  Taiwan dlr    32.945\tab  32.936\tab    -0.03\par  Kor