\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firmer as central banks lurk. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2001\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  clawed towards the stronger end of their recent ranges late Tuesday as the market kept a wary eye on central banks. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, Thai baht, and Korean won staved off further losses as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruled the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Thai and Korean authorities had again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defence of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , continuing a recent trend, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore reaffirmed its current monetary policy bias towards tightening. \par \par \uc2  The yen's mild rebound following cautionary remarks from a Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa also helped the regionals keep their footing. \par \par \uc2  But they were unable to muster enough strength to break past key resistance levels, with the yen still looking fragile over the longer term. \par \par \uc2  Adding more woe to the regional outlook, Singapore, one of Asia's sounder economies, turned in a weaker than expected first quarter performance, with growth of 4.6 percent on year against expectations of 5.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The city-state also revised downwards its 2001 growth forecast to 3.5-5.5 percent from 5-7 percent due to the slowdown in the U.S. and global electronics sector. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's economy also showed more symptoms of a slowdown with March exports falling 1.8 percent on year and imports down a substantial 13.1 percent. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its 2001 export growth forecast from 4.21 percent, adding import growth "should be negative." \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won reclaimed ground in late trade, helped by Korean authorities who were spotted selling dollars around 1,336 won. \par \par \uc2  The government has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market in recent sessions to push the dollar/won lower after several weeks of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Given the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the accompanying reluctance to hold dollar longs, analysts said dollar/won may retrace to 1,330. \par \par \uc2  The dollar/won's daily chart showed it was still within an uptrend channel that started on February 21, with support around the 1,330 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said there was some genuine demand for dollars from Korean importers and offshore parties that capped the won's gains. \par \par \uc2  They added that trade had thinned out due to wariness over increased government activity and the rangebound dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  "These levels are really hard to play because you're not quite sure whether the market is waiting for another big move in dollar/yen or for a big correction (in dollar/won)," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar edged up to 1.8132 in afternoon trading, after hovering at 1.8140-60 from earlier lows of 1.8200. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic U.S. dollar bids from foreign and local banks ran into fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  especially after it reaffirmed its tightening bias. \par \par \uc2  The MAS also said it stood ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to keep the Sing dollar within its policy band. \par \par \uc2  The MAS's comment came after the government announced a lower-than-expected growth figure for the first quarter and a bigger-than-expected cut in Singapore's 2001 growth forecast. Yet dealers expected the Sing dollar to soon revisit 1.8180 and 1.8200 lows on the back of burgeoning M&A activities which point to capital flows out of Singapore. But they saw no big orders related to talk DBS Group was making a bid for Dao Heng Bank in a deal valued at up to $5.78 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The talk is still very much up in the air and we haven't heard of any confirmation. On top of that, DBS is a bank. I think they are clever enough to hedge their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged higher from its session low of 10,875 as a lack of local corporate demand for dollars prompted banks to trim their dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said corporates were reluctant to bid dollars above 10,800 ahead of the start of an IMF review of Indonesia's performance on economic reforms on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The review is seen as a step towards resumption of IMF lending, stalled since December after the Fund said Jakarta failed to meet certain programme targets. \par \par \uc2  However, the rupiah's rise was capped at around 10,740 where some local banks were seen buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state banks were spotted selling dollars in early trade but given the small amount sold, most dealers suspected they were not acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Finance Minister said he saw no significant problems affecting the IMF review as all the key requirements demanded by the IMF had been met. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso firmed off a session low of 50.25 on inflows of overseas workers' remittances, bunched up with only two working days in the week. \par \par \uc2  Philippine markets were closed on Monday and will go on Easter break from Thursday. Trading will resume on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the dollar inflows mostly coming from local banks prompted others to trim their dollar longs and sent importers to the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  As expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left key interest rates steady at its weekly policy meeting. The overnight borrowing rate stands at 10.0 percent and the lending rate at 12.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank was not in the market to support the peso and attributed its recent weakness to regional declines and not to its easing policy. \par \par \uc2  A government source said the first quarter deficit was likely to come at around 37.054 billion pesos, below previous estimates of 48.552 billion. The Philippines has a 2001 budget deficit target of 145 billion pesos, against last year's 136.11 billion. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht traded in a narrow range in the afternoon following rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the offshore spot and forward markets through a U.S. name. \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  upstaged negative local factors. \par \par \uc2  Consumer confidence in the Thai economy fell for the second straight month in March from the previous month, according to a survey by the University of Thai Chamber of Commerce. \par \par \uc2  The commerce ministry also cut its 2001 export growth target to 9.45 percent year-on-year from 11.30 percent earlier and an actual 19.5 percent rise in 2000. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs offshore eased, with the one-month forward rate at 17/45 satang per dollar against 37/47 in the morning. TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar firmed slightly as most players opted for the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  With the yen holding above 125 and dollar selling in other Asian non-deliverable forwards, dealers said there were few incentives for the market to take on dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  However, further evidence of Taiwan's slowing economy kept a lid on the local dollar's upside. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry slashed its 2001 export growth forecast to 0.5 percent from 4.21 percent after the release of data showing a 1.8 percent on year fall in exports in March. Imports fell 13.1 percent on year in March. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0818 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.37\tab  125.21\tab    +0.68\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8145\tab  1.8155\tab    +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    32.927\tab  32.936\tab    +0.03\par  Korean won   1330.00\tab 1337.00\tab    +0.53\par  Baht\tab      45.58\tab   45.65\tab    +0.15\par  Peso\tab      49.91\tab   50.00\tab    +0.18\par  Rupiah\tab 10720.00     10791.00\tab    +0.66\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.37\tab  114.45\tab    -7.98\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8145\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.30\par  Taiwan dlr    32.927\tab  32.900\tab    -0.08\par  Korean won   1330.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -3.98\par  Baht\tab      45.58\tab   43.70\tab    -4.12\par  Peso\tab      49.91\tab   50.75\tab    +1.68\par  Rupiah\tab 10720.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -11.66\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4a029i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
