\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Stocks shadow U.S. slide,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  sag. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2001\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 9 (Reuters) - Asian equities ceded ground \par \par \uc2  on Monday as bleak job numbers and corporate profit warnings in \par \par \uc2  the United States fanned fresh fears about the outlook for \par \par \uc2  Asian economies. \par \par \uc2      The Nasdaq Composite Index slid 3.6 percent and the Dow \par \par \uc2  Jones Industrial Average shed 1.3 percent on Friday, leaving \par \par \uc2  stocks in Japan, Singapore and Malaysia as major casualties. \par \par \uc2      Japan's benchmark Nikkei average fell four percent, with \par \par \uc2  additional home-grown pessimism emerging from a disappointing \par \par \uc2  emergency stimulus package unveiled on Friday and a dip in \par \par \uc2  March domestic wholesale prices, fuelling doubts about Japan's \par \par \uc2  ability to shake off anaemic growth. \par \par \uc2      Singapore's Straits Times Index was the region's worst \par \par \uc2  performer, falling as much a five percent at one point to \par \par \uc2  breach the key 1,600 mark for the first time in two years. \par \par \uc2      Concerns about slowing export demand knocked Malaysia, with \par \par \uc2  the benchmark Composite Index losing 4.17 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also eased back against the U.S. dollar. The yen \par \par \uc2  lapsed a full yen to 124.94 yen from 123.82 on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drew marginal support from \par \par \uc2  wariness about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  BRACED FOR GDP RELEASE \par \par \uc2      Those fears kept the Sing dollar from revisiting decade \par \par \uc2  lows of 1.8235 hit last week, allowing it to hang around 1.8150 \par \par \uc2  over the course of the day. \par \par \uc2      The market was even more wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  after \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second finance minister was quoted at the \par \par \uc2  weekend as saying the authorities would continue to defend the \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar if it became too volatile. \par \par \uc2  The market is waiting with bated breath for a revised \par \par \uc2  growth forecast for 2001 and preliminary growth figures for the \par \par \uc2  first quarter due out on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll predicted the government would trim its \par \par \uc2  official forecast for 2001 growth to between four to six \par \par \uc2  percent, from its current estimate of five to seven percent. \par \par \uc2      This compares with growth of 9.9 percent last year, which \par \par \uc2  was mainly due to buoyant electronics exports. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said bleak numbers could confirm the need for the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to shift its monetary stance to \par \par \uc2  neutral from tightening. \par \par \uc2      Speculation was intense the MAS might have already shifted \par \par \uc2  its monetary stance given recent steep falls in the Sing dollar \par \par \uc2  amid a lack of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But some said the MAS may not need to do so as it manages \par \par \uc2  its exchange rate against a trade-weighted basket of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most of which crumpled against the dollar in line \par \par \uc2  with the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  "The Sing dollar can actually gain competitiveness without \par \par \uc2  having to shift that much, because it is managed on a very \par \par \uc2  broad-based basket," Chia Woon Khien, regional strategist at \par \par \uc2  Dresdner Bank Ag told the Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  If the U.S. dollar rose to 130 yen and other Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved 50-75 percent of that proportionately, she \par \par \uc2  said the Sing dollar would appreciate in relative terms, given \par \par \uc2  that the Malaysian ringgit - also a major component in its \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted basket - is pegged against the greenback. \par \par \uc2      "So I don't think there is need to panic on the dollar/Sing \par \par \uc2  that it would shoot past 1.85," Chia said. \par \par \uc2      INDONESIA AND THE IMF \par \par \uc2      Indonesia saw both its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks wallow despite \par \par \uc2  growing hopes a long-awaited mission by the International \par \par \uc2  Monetary Fund would help its limping economy. \par \par \uc2      The visit should pave the way for disbursement of a $400 \par \par \uc2  million loan delayed by the IMF since late last year and \par \par \uc2  trigger a $5.8 billion debt restructuring deal with the Paris \par \par \uc2  Club of official creditors. \par \par \uc2  But analysts cautioned about expecting too much from the \par \par \uc2  visit and said there were still many lingering economic \par \par \uc2  concerns such as controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law changes. \par \par \uc2  An independent panel reviewing planned reforms to \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws completed its work on Sunday but no details of its \par \par \uc2  findings have been released. \par \par \uc2  The government said on Monday it agreed in principle with \par \par \uc2  the results of the independent panel's review of planned \par \par \uc2  reforms to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0909 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.21\tab  124.87\tab    -0.27\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8155\tab  1.8158\tab    +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    32.936\tab  32.940\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1337.00\tab 1342.10\tab    +0.38\par  Baht\tab      45.65\tab   45.63\tab    -0.04\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.00\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab 10791.00     10850.00\tab    +0.55\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.21\tab  114.45\tab    -8.59\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8155\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.35\par  Taiwan dlr    32.936\tab  32.900\tab    -0.11\par  Korean won   1337.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -4.49\par  Baht\tab      45.65\tab   43.70\tab    -4.27\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.75\tab    +1.50\par  Rupiah\tab 10791.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -12.24\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0909 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  12841.76     13383.76\tab    -4.05\par  Hong Kong   12202.10     12386.61\tab    -1.49\par  Singapore    1594.95\tab 1670.18\tab    -4.50\par  Taipei\tab  5401.83\tab 5515.13\tab    -2.05\par  Seoul\tab    497.46\tab  506.22\tab    -1.73\par  Bangkok\tab  279.17\tab  282.02\tab    -1.01\par  Manila\tab  closed\tab  1471.13\tab      N/A\par  Jakarta\tab  362.28\tab  364.34\tab    -0.57\par  Kuala Lumpur  553.34\