\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steadier, but bleak U.S. data weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2001\par 03:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 9 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained their composure in early trade on Monday as players cashed in on recent dollar gains, but a weak yen and poor U.S. employment data kept them vulnerable to downside risks. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. March jobs report showed a decline of 86,000 in non-farm payroll jobs versus an expected increase of 58,000 jobs. The unemployment rate matched expectations for a rise to 4.3 percent but was the highest since mid-1999. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the numbers stoked fears of a U.S. recession and that worry was likely to weigh on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Asian countries whose growth depends a great deal on exports to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  "I see medium-term softness for the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which can be attributed to both internal and external factors. Firstly, you need the U.S. to be confident about itself before Asia can be confident about its outlook," said Philip Wee, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "And you cannot blame the U.S. or the yen alone. Asian countries seem to have missed the opportunity to reform. And unless they push harder for it, their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to be pressured," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the region, Singapore is scheduled to release a flash estimate of its January-March economic growth, along with its revised forecast for growth domestic product in 2001 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast the economy grew 5.9 percent in the first quarter and are predicting growth on average of 4.6 percent in 2001, hurt by a slowdown in the U.S. and global technology demand. \par \par \uc2  Philippine markets are closed for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won steadied with the help of the firmer yen and wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  State banks were spotted selling dollars heavily on Friday, pulling the won off the day's low of 1,358.5. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea was believed to be behind the dollar selling. The bank kept rates steady at its monthly policy meeting on Friday, citing growing inflationary pressures due to rising consumer prices and a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, while the market was erring on the side of caution following Friday's activity, analysts said the BOK was unlikely to step up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen headed south again. \par \par \uc2  "But while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks have undoubtedly increased, the authorities are aware that their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves can quickly begin to fall ... Moreover, the authorities will not want to hurt the competitiveness of Korean exporters," said a UBS Warburg report. \par \par \uc2  It also noted the Korean authorities had allowed the won to weaken against the yen. The yen/won cross rate was at 10.78 at 0030 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry announced on Saturday the government would redo its marcroeconomic targets, adding it would also curb hikes in public service charges that have been blamed for the increase in inflation. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was steady in early trade in line with other regionals and on wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but dealers said local corporates were likely to chase the dollar up to test 10,900 again. \par \par \uc2  The market will also keep an eye on the IMF mission which is due to begin a much-awaited review of Jakarta's performance on agreed targets under a funding programme. \par \par \uc2  Differences with the IMF on proposed changes to laws governing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  became more obvious when Attorney-General Marzuki Darusman said on Saturday the IMF was overstepping itself by insisting Article 75 be dropped. \par \par \uc2  Article 75 stipulates that the whole board of Bank Indonesia resign once the new law takes effect. \par \par \uc2  The controversial changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law are among the the major reasons the IMF has withheld disbursement of a $400 million loan tranche since December. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso held steady in light offshore trade with markets in Manila closed for the Valour Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the peso was likely to stay under pressure in the near term with exporters and overseas workers holding back dollars due to the weaker regional outlook. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said at the weekend commercial banks should aim to build up their loan-loss provisions to cover more than 60 percent of bad loans. \par \par \uc2  At end-January, commercial banks' non-performing loan ratio rose to 16 percent of total loans from 15.1 percent in December. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar posted some gains as the market kept a close eye on the yen's moves, but Taipei dealers said its upside was being capped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was spotted buying dollars on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said inflation data issued on Friday showed room for looser monetary policy, meaning the local dollar could weaken further. Consumer prices rose a tame 0.44 percent on year in March against February's 1.02 percent on year fall. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut rates repeatedly since December, citing relatively subdued inflation. \par \par \uc2  With external demand slowing, analysts said the bank was seeking to boost the domestic economy while maintaining the competitiveness of Taiwan's exports. \par \par \uc2  "With the economy sluggish and Asian competitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluing substantially, the CBC (Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will have to let the Taiwan dollar adjust as well in order to maintain economic growth," said UBS Warburg in a research note. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing bounced half a cent to 1.8120 in early trading from Friday's lows of 1.8184, thanks to the firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said bears were reluctant to push the Sing dollar lower given its four-percent loss since the beginning of the year, due to concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Such fears were rekindled after media reports quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second finance minister Lim Hng Kiang telling reporters at the weekend ASEAN meeting the authorities would continue to defend the Sing dollar if it became too volatile. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said U.S. names were eager to bid up dollar/Sing, with large orders around 1.8110-30. \par \par \uc2  The market is keeping a wary eye on a revised growth forecast for 2001 and preliminary growth figures for the first quarter due out on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was looking vulnerable at 45.60, not far from fresh 37-month lows of 45.72 hit in light offshore trade on Friday when Thai markets were closed. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said both onshore and offshore banks were looking to bid dollar/baht up, with 45.50 seen as good support. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said late on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not allow speculation in the baht and he did not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would reach 47 or 48 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak added to a string of official warnings, saying on Sunday he expected volatility in the baht to be short-lived. \par \par \uc2  He added interest rates could ease soon if the national asset management company can resolve bad loan problems. The benchmark 14-day repo rate currently stands at 1.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The AMC plans to take over a portion of 1.7 trillion baht in non-performing loans from banks and push ahead with restructuring. \par \par \uc2  Offshore baht funding costs were still firm with the one-month forward rate at 40/45 satang per dollar against 30/40 late on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0131 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.60\tab  124.87\tab    +0.22\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8140\tab  1.8158\tab    +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    32.942\tab  32.940\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1342.10\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      45.64\tab   45.63\tab    -0.02\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.00\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab 10850.00     10850.00\tab    +0.00\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.60\tab  114.45\tab    -8.15\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8140\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.27\par  Taiwan dlr    32.942\tab  32.900\tab    -0.13\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -4.85\par  Baht\tab      45.64\tab   43.70\tab    -4.25\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.75\tab    +1.